window.DOC_SEARCH = [["accordion","Accordion","","Accordion","Sections that open and close, built on <details> : also without JavaScript, from the keyboard and with screen readers.",""],["accordion","Accordion","accordion","Accordion","A list of sections that open and close, built on the native <details> element: it works without JavaScript, is used from the keyboard (Enter and Space on the title) and is already readable by screen readers. The container is kit-accordion , each item is a direct-child <details> with a <summary> as the title and the content inside kit-accordion-body . open on the <details> opens it initially. Where the browser supports it the opening is animated (not with \"reduce motion\"). How do I issue an invoice? From the Invoices menu choose \"New\", fill in the customer and lines and save: the number is assigned automatically. Can I edit it after sending? No: a sent invoice is corrected with a credit note and a new invoice. Where do I find rejected invoices? In the list, with the \"Discarded\" filter. The reason for the rejection is in the detail.","kit-accordion kit-accordion-body"],["accordion","Accordion","accordion-single","Only one open","data-kit-accordion=\"single\" (requires kit.js ) closes the other items when one is opened; if several items start open only the first stays open. Without JavaScript the same effect is achieved with the same name=\"…\" on all the <details> , which recent browsers honor by themselves. An accordion inside another's item is independent. Company details Company name, VAT number and address. Contacts Email, certified email and phone. Payments IBAN and payment terms.","data-kit-accordion kit-accordion kit-accordion-body"],["accordion","Accordion","accordion-meta","With a label and inside a card","kit-accordion-meta inside the <summary> puts a count or a badge on the right, before the arrow. kit-accordion-flush removes the box and shadows, for an accordion inside a card or a panel. To issue 3 Three draft invoices. Discarded 1 One invoice rejected by the exchange system. Archived 128 Invoices from previous years.","kit-accordion-meta kit-accordion-flush kit-card kit-card-body kit-accordion kit-badge kit-badge-warning kit-accordion-body kit-badge-danger"],["accordion","Accordion","accordion-js","JavaScript","Kit.accordion(element, { single }) does the same from code and returns { open(x), close(x), toggle(x), openAll(), closeAll(), items() } , where x is the position (from 0) or the <details> . Every opening and closing fires kit:accordion with { item, index, open } . When printing all items are shown open. const acc = Kit.accordion(\"#faq\", { single: true }); acc.open(2); // opens the third item (and closes the others) acc.closeAll(); document.querySelector(\"#faq\").addEventListener(\"kit:accordion\", (e) => { console.log(e.detail.index, e.detail.open); });","Kit.accordion kit-code data-kit-code"],["buttons","Buttons","","Buttons","Buttons of all kinds and sizes. A .kit-btn works on <button> , <a> and <label> .",""],["buttons","Buttons","variants","Variants","Default Primary Ghost Danger Disabled kit-btn-primary for the screen's main action (only one per area), kit-btn-ghost for secondary actions without a border, kit-btn-danger for destructive ones.","kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-danger"],["buttons","Buttons","sizes","Sizes","The base height is --kit-ctl (40px), the same as fields, so buttons and inputs line up. kit-btn-lg brings it to 48px. Normal Large","--kit-ctl kit-btn-lg kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["buttons","Buttons","icons","With an icon","Put the <svg class=\"kit-icon\"> before the text. For icon-only buttons add kit-btn-icon (square) and an aria-label . Download","kit-icon kit-btn-icon kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost"],["buttons","Buttons","counter","With a counter","Filters 3","kit-btn kit-count"],["buttons","Buttons","group","Group and link","One Two A link","kit-btn-group kit-btn"],["cards","Cards and details","","Cards and details","Cards, KPI cards, stats row, lists, key/value pairs and code blocks: the containers and details of a dashboard.",""],["cards","Cards and details","card","Card","A container with a border, rounded corners and a light shadow (in the dark theme the shadow disappears). Every part is optional: kit-card-head , kit-card-body , kit-card-foot . Card title The card content. Cancel Save Without kit-card-body the content touches the edges: fine for full-width tables and charts.","kit-card-head kit-card-body kit-card-foot kit-card kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["cards","Cards and details","kpi","KPI card","A label, a big value and a change. In a row with kit-row-cols-* add kit-h-100 so they all reach the same height. Documents 1,284 +4% Total €48,920.10 +1.2% To review 17 −3 Discarded 2 +1","kit-row-cols kit-h-100 kit-row kit-row-cols-2 kit-row-cols-lg-4 kit-card kit-kpi kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-badge-warning kit-badge-danger"],["cards","Cards and details","stats","Stats row","More compact than KPIs: many figures in a single card, separated by a thin line. On the phone they stack. Documents 1,284 Total €48,920.10 VAT included Received €32,100 Issued €16,820","kit-card kit-stats kit-stat kit-success kit-danger"],["cards","Cards and details","list","List","Items stacked in the same box, like several joined cards: kit-list on the container, kit-list-item on each item. The container can be <ul> , <ol> or <div> ; the items <li> , <a> , <button> or <div> . A badge or an icon inside the item aligns by itself; kit-list-main gathers title and description and takes the free space. Received invoices Issued invoices 12 Credit notes Last imported yesterday 3","kit-list kit-list-item kit-list-main kit-badge kit-badge-warning"],["cards","Cards and details","list-actions","Clickable items","With <a> or <button> the item highlights on mouse hover. is-active (or aria-current ) marks the selected one, aria-disabled=\"true\" the unavailable one. The container, in this case, is a <div> . Overview Exports Settings Trash","kit-list kit-list-item kit-icon"],["cards","Cards and details","list-states","States","To signal an item's outcome: kit-list-item-success , -warning and -danger give a soft background and colored text. Import completed 2 documents to review 1 file discarded","kit-list-item-success kit-list kit-list-item kit-list-item-warning kit-list-item-danger"],["cards","Cards and details","list-cards","Separate cards and compact","kit-list-cards separates the items: each becomes a card with its own border, with a gap in between. It also works with clickable and active items and with the states. kit-list-sm reduces the space above and below each item and combines with the other variants. Smith Ltd Invoice 24/118 To pay Brown & Co. Invoice 24/119 Paid Green Inc Rejected by the tax authority Compact item Another compact item 2","kit-list-cards kit-list-sm kit-list kit-list-item kit-list-main kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-list-item-danger"],["cards","Cards and details","list-variants","Numbered, horizontal, borderless","kit-list-numbered puts a number in front of each item. kit-list-horizontal lays them out in a row, of equal width (below 760px they stack again). kit-list-flush removes border, corners and shadow: it is for use inside a card, which already has its own box. Choose the files Check the preview Confirm the import Draft Sent Paid Recent activity Smith Ltd Invoice 24/118 €1,250.00 Brown & Co. Invoice 24/119 €380.40","kit-list-numbered kit-list-horizontal kit-list-flush kit-list kit-list-item kit-card kit-card-head kit-list-main"],["cards","Cards and details","kv","Key / value","A two-column <dl> : gray labels, values on the right, with automatic wrapping for long texts. Useful for an item's details. Number FT-0042 Date 03/12/2026 Customer Alpha Services Ltd Description Consulting and support for the month of March, with reimbursement of travel expenses.","kit-card kit-card-body kit-kv"],["cards","Cards and details","code","Code snippets","A code block colored like in an editor: tags, attributes, strings, keywords, functions and comments. You write a normal <pre class=\"kit-code\"> and with data-kit-code (with kit.js ) the code colors itself. The value is the language: html (also with <script> and <style> inside), js or css ; without it, kit.js guesses. The text must be written with entities ( &lt; instead of < ), as in any HTML page. Without kit.js the block stays readable, just without colors. <button class=\"kit-btn kit-btn-primary\" data-kit-open=\"#new\"> <svg class=\"kit-icon\"><use href=\"#i-plus\"/></svg> New invoice </button> // reload the documents and show the outcome const n = await loadDocuments({ year: 2026, max: 50 }); Kit.toast(n + \" documents\", { type: \"success\" }); .invoice:hover { background: var(--kit-hover); } @media (max-width: 760px) { .invoice { padding: 8px; } }","kit-code data-kit-code kit-stack kit-btn kit-btn-primary data-kit-open kit-icon Kit.toast --kit-hover"],["cards","Cards and details","code-copy","The \"Copy\" button","With data-kit-code-copy the block is put in a kit-snippet and the \"Copy\" button appears (on mouse hover, always visible on the phone). The attribute's value is the label; data-kit-code-copied is the one that appears after copying. When the text is copied the kit:copy event fires with { text } . <section class=\"kit-card\"> <div class=\"kit-card-body\">Hello</div> </section>","data-kit-code-copy kit-snippet data-kit-code-copied kit-code data-kit-code kit-card kit-card-body"],["cards","Cards and details","code-js","From JavaScript","Kit.code(pre, { lang, text, copy }) colors a block and returns { set(text, lang), text() } , useful when the code changes (a generated example, a preview). Kit.highlight(text, lang) instead returns an already colored DOM fragment, to insert wherever you like. Both build only text nodes and <span> s, never HTML: the displayed code is not executed, whatever it contains. Beyond 100,000 characters the text stays uncolored, so a huge text does not slow the page; an unknown language is guessed. const block = Kit.code(\"#example\", { lang: \"js\", copy: true }); block.set(\"Kit.toast('Saved!');\"); // changes the displayed code element.append(Kit.highlight(\"<b>hello</b>\", \"html\")); The colors are the tokens --kit-hl-tag , -attr , -str , -kw , -fn , -num e -com (see Themes and tokens ), and change by themselves between light and dark theme.","Kit.code Kit.highlight kit-code data-kit-code Kit.toast --kit-hl-tag"],["charts","Charts","","Charts","Bars, lines, donut and sparklines in SVG, no libraries. They require kit.js .",""],["charts","Charts","bars","Bar chart","Kit.barChart(element, options) draws a bar chart in SVG inside the element. The vertical axis has round values (1, 2, 2.5, 5, 10 for a power of ten) with thousands abbreviated as \"k\" and \"M\". Each bar has a tooltip. If there are many bars the chart scrolls horizontally and starts from the end, that is, from the most recent data. Colors, texts and grid follow the theme and the text size; the chart redraws itself when the window changes width. Each element of data has a label ( label ), a value for each series ( values ) and, optionally, a group : it is written under the bar only when it changes, and is handy for the year. v.toLocaleString(\"en-US\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"EUR\" }) });'>","Kit.barChart"],["charts","Charts","series","Several series and clicks","With several series ( series ) each month has one bar per series and the legend appears. The default colors are --kit-c1 … --kit-c4 ; for another color there is color in the series. With onSelect the bars become buttons reachable with Tab, activated with Enter or space; the element also receives the kit:select event with { index, series, item } . Kit.toast(\"Month: \" + month.label + \" \" + month.group) });'>","--kit-c1 --kit-c4 Kit.barChart Kit.toast"],["charts","Charts","stacked","Stacked bars","stacked: true puts the series one on top of the other: each month has a single bar, as tall as the sum. Useful to see how a total is made up.","Kit.barChart"],["charts","Charts","lines","Lines","Kit.lineChart takes the same options as bars. A null value leaves a gap in the line (the month without data). The axis starts from the lowest value, not from zero, so variations are visible; zero: true brings it back to zero. Each series has a different symbol (circle, square, triangle), so they can be told apart even without the colors. area: true colors the space under the line, markers: false removes the points. v.toFixed(3) + \" €/l\", axisFormat: (v) => v.toFixed(2) + \" €\" });'>","Kit.lineChart"],["charts","Charts","donut","Donut","Kit.donut shows the parts of a total. In the center is the total (or the text of centerValue and centerLabel ), beside it a legend with value and percentage. With onSelect the legend rows become buttons. Slices with a value of zero do not appear. v.toLocaleString(\"en-US\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"EUR\", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }), centerLabel: \"Spending 2026\" });'>","Kit.donut --kit-mute"],["charts","Charts","legend","Chart legend","The series colors are the --kit-c1 and --kit-c2 tokens, which change by themselves between light and dark theme. In SVG charts use them with fill: var(--kit-c1) (see the sample dashboard ). Received Issued","--kit-c1 --kit-c2 kit-legend"],["charts","Charts","sparkline","Sparkline","Kit.sparkline is a tiny chart, with no axes, to put next to a number, for example in a KPI card . It takes values and, optionally, type ( \"line\" or \"bar\" ), color , area ( false removes it) and label . The size is that of the element: change it with CSS (by default 6rem × 1.9rem). Invoices 22 Refuellings 5","Kit.sparkline --kit-c2 kit-stats kit-kpi kit-mute kit-fs-3 kit-fw-bold"],["charts","Charts","options","Bar and line options","Option Values Default data array of { label, group?, values: [n, …] } – series array of { name, color? } one \"Total\" series label description for screen reader users Bar chart format function for the values in tooltips number with the page language's separators axisFormat function for the axis values abbreviation with \"k\" and \"M\" height · ticks · minSlot height in px, number of lines, minimum width of a column in px 260 · 4 · 34 max maximum value of the axis computed from the data, rounded legend · legendNote true / false · text added to the legend legend only with several series stacked (bars) stacked series false area · markers · zero (lines) colored area · points · axis from zero false · true · false min minimum value of the axis 0 for bars, computed for lines scrollEnd starts from the last bar when scrolling true onSelect (elemento, indice, serie) => … none: bars are not clickable empty text if data is empty No data The function returns { update(options), destroy() } . Calling it again on the same element updates the existing chart: Kit.barChart(el, { data: newData }) changes only the data. Negative values are not supported in bars (they are drawn as zero). All four functions (","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table Kit.barChart kit-chart --kit-c1 --kit-c4 --kit-line --kit-mute kit-chart-bar kit-chart-axis kit-chart-label kit-chart-group"],["dates","Dates and times","","Dates and times","Date and time fields with the kit's look, an optional calendar for a date, a range, date and time, and time only. Designed for the phone: on narrow screens the calendar slides up from the bottom, with 44-pixel targets.",""],["dates","Dates and times","native","Native fields",".kit-input also works on date , time , datetime-local , month and week : the same height, border and focus ring as the other fields, aligned numbers and, on iOS, left-aligned text and the right height even when the field is empty. No JavaScript is needed: the picker is the browser's, which on a phone is usually the best. Min and max ( min , max ) and aria-invalid=\"true\" work as for the other fields. Date Time Date and time Month Week Invalid date The date cannot be in the past. For a range without JavaScript a kit-daterange container with two fields is enough: they sit in a single frame, separated by a line. Period (browser picker)","kit-input kit-fields kit-field kit-danger kit-daterange"],["dates","Dates and times","calendar","Calendar","With data-kit-datepicker on the field (needs kit.js ) the browser's picker gives way to a calendar that is the same everywhere. It is optional: without the attribute the field stays native, and without JavaScript the one with the attribute stays a normal type=\"date\" . The field shows and accepts mm/dd/yyyy (the order follows the page's language : in Italian it is dd/mm/yyyy ). You can also type it: the slashes are added by themselves and 3/5/26 , 03.05.2026 , 03052026 , 2026-03-05 all work. The value sent with the form is always yyyy-mm-dd , in a hidden field that takes the name : the server reads it without conversions. It opens with the calendar button or the down arrow. On a phone you just tap the field (the keyboard does not appear). The month title leads to the months, and the year title to the years: useful for birth dates. Issue date Due date Value: – On change the field's input and change events fire (so htmx's hx-trigger=\"change\" works too) and kit:change with { value, display } : value in ISO, display as written in the field.","data-kit-datepicker kit-fields kit-field kit-input"],["dates","Dates and times","limits","Limits and excluded days","min and max (or data-kit-min and data-kit-max ) set the allowed range. Besides the ISO date they accept today and an offset in days: +30 is in thirty days, -7 a week ago. data-kit-disable excludes days of the week ( mon … sun ) and specific dates. Excluded days are visible but cannot be chosen; if the date is typed by hand the field is invalid ( setCustomValidity , so the form does not submit) and gets the red border. Delivery (from today, Monday to Friday) Within 90 days, excluding Saturday, Sunday and Christmas. Date of birth For distant years: month title, then year title.","data-kit-min data-kit-max data-kit-disable kit-fields kit-field kit-input data-kit-datepicker"],["dates","Dates and times","range","Range","data-kit-daterange on a container with two <input type=\"date\"> (from, to). The calendar shows two months side by side, with a colored band between the two dates; while choosing the second one, hovering over the days shows a preview. You can also type the dates in the two fields. If \"to\" precedes \"from\" the field is invalid. The quick choices are on the left (on a phone they become a scrolling row above the calendar); data-kit-presets chooses which ones ( none removes them). Period Value: 2026-11-01 → 2026-11-12 The available choices are today , yesterday , 7 , 30 , 90 (last N days), month , last-month , year , last-year (the old Italian names oggi , ieri , mese , mese-scorso , anno , anno-scorso still work). By default 7,30,month,last-month,year . Those that fall outside min and max are shortened, or disabled if they stay entirely outside. The kit:change event has { from, to } , and input and change fire on both fields.","data-kit-daterange data-kit-presets kit-field kit-daterange kit-input"],["dates","Dates and times","datetime","Date and time","On a type=\"datetime-local\" the calendar has hour and minute columns next to it. The field shows mm/dd/yyyy hh:mm and sends yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm , like the native field. \"Done\" closes. If you only choose the time, the date becomes today; if you only choose the day, the time is 00:00. data-kit-step=\"15\" (minutes) limits the minutes to multiples of 15; the step attribute in seconds works too. Appointment Value: 2026-11-12T09:30","data-kit-step kit-fields kit-field kit-input data-kit-datepicker"],["dates","Dates and times","time","Time only","On a type=\"time\" (or with data-kit-timepicker ) you choose hours and minutes in two columns. You can also type 9 , 9.30 , 930 . The value is hh:mm in 24 hours, the same as the native field. min and max count as times ( 09:00 , 18:00 ). Opening Value: 09:00","data-kit-timepicker kit-fields kit-field kit-input data-kit-step"],["dates","Dates and times","phone","Phone and touch","Below 576 px the calendar becomes a bottom sheet , full width, with a darkened backdrop and a \"Close\" button; the backdrop edge or Esc closes it. The page below does not scroll. With a \"coarse\" pointer (fingers) days, months and hours are 44 px tall, even on a tablet. The field does not open the keyboard ( inputmode=\"none\" ): a tap opens the calendar. With a mouse it stays a numeric field to type in. The field's text is at least 16 px, so iOS does not zoom the page. The calendar is in the page's top layer ( popover ): no card, scrolling table or dialog clips it. If you prefer the system picker for phones, do not add data-kit-datepicker and use the native field: its look is already the kit's. Date fields inside a dialog","data-kit-datepicker kit-bar kit-btn data-kit-open kit-dialog kit-card-head"],["dates","Dates and times","dlg-date-t","New appointment","Day Time Close","kit-card-body kit-fields kit-field kit-input data-kit-datepicker data-kit-timepicker kit-card-foot kit-btn data-kit-close"],["dates","Dates and times","keyboard","Keyboard","Where Keys Field ↓ opens the calendar; you can type the date. Tab leaves the field. Days ← → one day, ↑ ↓ one week, Home and End start and end of the week, PageUp and PageDown one month, Shift + PageUp/PageDown one year. Enter or Space choose. Months and years Arrows to move, Enter to choose. Hours and minutes ↑ ↓ in the column, ← → from one column to the other, Home and End for the first and the last. Open calendar Esc closes and returns focus to the field. Tab goes through the controls and leaves from the last one.","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table"],["dates","Dates and times","options","Attributes and options","Attribute JS option What it does data-kit-datepicker type Calendar on the field. The type ( date , datetime , time ) is read from type=\"date|datetime-local|time\" ; on a text field you write the value: data-kit-datepicker=\"datetime\" . data-kit-timepicker – As above, for time only. data-kit-daterange – On a container with two date fields (from, to). min , max (or data-kit-min , -max ) min , max on the field Limits: ISO, today , +N or -N days; for times hh:mm . data-kit-disable disable Excluded days: sat,sun,2026-12-25 ; from JavaScript also a function (iso) => true . data-kit-step or step step Minutes step (1–30). 1 by default. data-kit-presets presets Quick choices for the range (a list, or none ). required – The field is required and the calendar does not offer \"Clear\".","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-datepicker data-kit-timepicker data-kit-daterange data-kit-min data-kit-disable data-kit-step data-kit-presets"],["dates","Dates and times","django","With Django and htmx","The visible field has no name : the hidden one has it, and it contains the ISO date. So request.GET[\"dal\"] and cleaned_data receive 2026-11-12 , with no formats to configure. # forms.py — format=\"%Y-%m-%d\" lets the native field (without JavaScript) show the initial value class PeriodForm(forms.Form): dal = forms.DateField(required=False, widget=forms.DateInput( format=\"%Y-%m-%d\", attrs={\"type\": \"date\", \"class\": \"kit-input\", \"aria-label\": \"From\"})) al = forms.DateField(required=False, widget=forms.DateInput( format=\"%Y-%m-%d\", attrs={\"type\": \"date\", \"class\": \"kit-input\", \"aria-label\": \"To\"})) <form hx-get=\"{% url 'invoices' %}\" hx-target=\"#results\" hx-trigger=\"change\"> <div class=\"kit-daterange\" data-kit-daterange>{{ form.dal }}{{ form.al }}</div> </form> With htmx put hx-get and hx-trigger=\"change\" on the form (or a container), not on the single field: the hidden field is in the form and gets included. The change event fires after every choice, with the value already updated. On a single field, hx-include names the other one. The fragments htmx inserts initialize by themselves ( htmx:load ); also with hx-swap=\"outerHTML\" on the form. With django-filter, DateFromToRangeFilter and Ra","kit-code data-kit-code kit-input kit-daterange data-kit-daterange kit-danger"],["dates","Dates and times","js","JavaScript","const field = Kit.datepicker(\"#due\"); // returns { get, set, clear, open, close } field.set(\"2026-12-31\"); // without an event (set(v, true) fires it) field.get(); // \"2026-12-31\" const period = Kit.daterange(\"#period\", { presets: [\"today\", \"7\", \"month\"] }); period.set({ from: \"2026-11-01\", to: \"2026-11-12\" }); period.get(); // { from, to } Kit.date.parse(\"3/5/26\"); // \"2026-03-05\" (\"\" if empty, null if not a date; the order depends on the language) Kit.date.format(\"2026-03-05\"); // \"03/05/2026\" Kit.i18n.add(\"en\", { date: { t: { today: \"Now\" } } }); // texts and month names can be replaced (see Languages) document.addEventListener(\"kit:change\", (e) => { console.log(e.detail); // { value, display } or { from, to } }); Dates are ISO strings and calculations are done in UTC, so the browser's time zone never shifts a day. \"Today\" is the device's local date.","kit-code data-kit-code Kit.datepicker Kit.daterange Kit.date Kit.i"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","","Alerts and progress","Alerts, status badges, progress bars, empty states and a welcome screen.",""],["feedback","Alerts and progress","alerts","Alerts","A highlighted message inside the page: colored left border and soft background. Without a variant it is information; the others are -success , -warning , -danger and -neutral . Imported invoices stay on your computer. Import completed: 24 invoices added. 3 invoices are waiting for a receipt from the tax authority. Unable to read the file: it is not a valid invoice. Last updated: today at 09:41. With an icon Put a <svg class=\"kit-icon kit-alert-icon\"> as the first child: the alert leaves room on the left and the icon takes the variant's color. Icons come from your SVG sprite; here i-info , i-ok , i-warn and i-error (you will find them in this documentation's sprite). Imported invoices stay on your computer. Import completed: 24 invoices added. 3 invoices are waiting for a receipt from the tax authority. Unable to read the file: it is not a valid invoice. For an important alert use role=\"alert\" (it is read immediately by screen readers), for the others role=\"status\" . With a title and a link Deadline approaching You have until the 30th of the month. Go to the invoices to send . Dismissible A .kit-alert-close button with data-kit-dismiss removes the alert. The kit:dismiss event bubble","kit-stack kit-alert kit-alert-success kit-alert-warning kit-alert-danger kit-alert-neutral kit-icon kit-alert-icon kit-alert-title kit-alert-close data-kit-dismiss"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","badge","Badge","Status labels. Color conveys the outcome: green positive, yellow needs checking, red error, gray neutral. Info Issued Received Error Neutral Do not rely on color alone for meaning: the badge's text must be enough on its own.","kit-bar kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-badge-warning kit-badge-danger kit-badge-neutral kit-alert"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","progress","Progress bar","Progress is the --kit-value variable (0–100%) on the inner element. Change it from JavaScript with el.style.setProperty(\"--kit-value\", \"40%\") .","--kit-value kit-stack kit-progress"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","meter","Meter","A measure against a limit: space used, plan quota, score. It differs from the progress bar because it is not heading toward completion: the value is what it is, and the color says whether the level is fine ( is-success ), needs attention ( is-warning ) or is critical ( is-danger ). Without a state class the bar is in the accent color. As with the native <meter> element, it has role=\"meter\" and its aria-valuenow , -min and -max ; the accessible label is aria-label . CSS only (fine for server-side rendering): the width is --kit-value and you choose the state. kit-meter-head puts name and value above the bar. Storage 32 GB of 100 Requests this month 430 of 500 Seats taken 48 of 50 With kit.js just give the value and thresholds and the state is computed by itself. The attributes are data-kit-value , data-kit-min (0), data-kit-max (100), data-kit-warn and data-kit-danger , in the same unit as the value. By default higher is worse: from warn up it is orange, from danger up red, below it is green. With data-kit-good=\"high\" (a score, a coverage) it reads the other way round: up to warn orange, up to danger red. Without thresholds it stays in the accent color. Meters inside a fragment inser","--kit-value kit-meter-head kit-stack kit-meter data-kit-value data-kit-min data-kit-max data-kit-warn data-kit-danger data-kit-good kit-meter-sm kit-meter-lg data-kit-meter Kit.meter kit-alert"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","spinner","Spinner","A spinning ring, in the text color and as big as the font: inside a button or next to a sentence nothing else is needed. kit-spinner-sm and -lg change the size, kit-spinner-accent uses the accent color. Add role=\"status\" and an aria-label , or text next to it, so that screen reader users know something is loading. Importing… Loading documents…","kit-spinner-sm kit-spinner-accent kit-bar kit-spinner kit-spinner-lg kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-mute"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","skeleton","Skeleton","Placeholders with a moving shine, to reserve space while data arrives. Put aria-busy=\"true\" on the container and aria-hidden=\"true\" on the placeholders, which are purely decorative. Parts: kit-skeleton-text (a line of text, the last one shorter), -title , -circle and -block .","kit-skeleton-text kit-card kit-card-body kit-d-flex kit-gap-3 kit-skeleton kit-skeleton-circle kit-skeleton-title"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","full-progress","Full-screen progress","For a long operation (reading a folder, importing a file) that blocks the rest of the page. Kit.progress(text, options) opens a dialog with the text and the bar and returns { update(text, value), close() } . The value goes from 0 to 1; without a value ( null ) the bar runs by itself, for when you do not know how much is left. Esc and a click on the background do not close it: you close it with close() , or with onCancel a \"Cancel\" button appears (and Esc counts as Cancel). With delay (in ms) it appears only if the operation lasts longer than that, so quick operations do not flash. Kit.toast(\"Reading cancelled\") }); for (let i = 1; i <= 40; i++) { await readInvoice(i); p.update(\"Reading \" + i + \" of 40\", i / 40); } p.close();'> With progress Without a value Option Values Default 1st argument the text above the bar empty value from 0 to 1, or null for the running bar null delay milliseconds before showing it 0 onCancel · cancel function called if the user cancels · button text none: it cannot be cancelled · Cancel","Kit.progress kit-bar Kit.toast kit-btn kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","empty","Empty state","When a list or table has nothing to show yet, explain why and what to do. 🗂️ No results Try changing the filters or searching for another term. Clear filters","kit-card kit-empty kit-empty-icon kit-btn"],["feedback","Alerts and progress","hero","Welcome screen","kit-hero centers a message with a few buttons: the first screen when there is no data yet. Explore your data Open a file to get started. Nothing leaves your computer. Open a file…","kit-hero kit-card kit-mute kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-lg"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","","Forms: select and file","Custom select, file field, drop zone and combobox: the controls that need kit.js .",""],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","select","Custom select","A dropdown menu with items, groups and a second line of text. It needs kit.js . On change the kit:change event fires (see JavaScript ). For a plain <select> just use class=\"kit-input\" . Period Quarters 1st quarter 2nd quarter April – June 3rd quarter Value: q1 The option with is-on is the initial one. kit-pop-right on the panel aligns it to the right of the button.","kit-input kit-field kit-select data-kit-select kit-select-btn kit-select-value kit-icon kit-pop kit-pop-group kit-opt kit-opt-text kit-opt-check kit-pop-right"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","native-select","From a native select","If the data is already in a <select> (even one generated by the server, inside a form, with required ) just add data-kit-select to it: the kit hides it and puts a button and menu next to it. The <select> stays the source of the data: value , form submission and the change event work as usual ( kit:change also fires, with { value, label } ). Use <optgroup> for groups; data-kit-hint on an option adds a second line and data-kit-short a shorter text for the button. From 21 items up the menu has a search field ( data-kit-search=\"8\" changes the threshold, data-kit-search=\"\" always shows it, data-kit-search=\"off\" never). Options and disabled can be changed later: the kit notices. Document type TD01 TD04 TD16 Not available Value: TD01","data-kit-select data-kit-hint data-kit-short data-kit-search kit-field"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","multiple-select","Multiple choice","A <select multiple data-kit-select> becomes a menu where each click toggles an item and the menu stays open (Esc or a click outside closes it). The button shows the chosen labels up to 2 ( data-kit-multi-max , or the multiMax option), then \"N selected\". The search field, groups, data-kit-hint and the keyboard (arrows, Enter or Space to toggle) work as in the single select. The <select> stays the source of the data: all the chosen values are submitted by the form, and change fires on every toggle. kit:change carries { value, values, labels } , where value and values are the arrays of the chosen values. Shops Alpha Ltd Beta Inc Gamma Transport Delta Supplies From JavaScript: Kit.select(el, { search, empty, placeholder }) does the same for a select added later ( Kit.init(root) does it for all those inside root ) and returns { sync(), open(), close() } . If you change select.value from code, call sync() to update the button (a change fired by hand already does).","data-kit-select data-kit-multi-max data-kit-hint kit-field data-kit-search Kit.select Kit.init"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","file","File field","A field to choose one or more files: a button, the name of the chosen file and an \"×\" to remove it. It needs kit.js (without it, the browser's native field stays). Write a normal <input type=\"file\"> inside kit-file with data-kit-file ; accept and multiple work as usual. The kit checks the type and, with data-kit-file-max (in MB), the size, and shows the error below the field. The files also stay in the form's field, so normal submission works. Invoices Accepts XML and P7M, up to 2 MB each.","kit-file data-kit-file data-kit-file-max kit-field"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","dropzone","Drop zone","The same thing, bigger: an area where you drag files, or click to choose. The native field covers the whole area, so the keyboard works (Tab and Enter). With data-kit-file-dir (or webkitdirectory on the field) it also accepts folders, which are read in full: files of another type are silently ignored, while a file of another type chosen directly gives an error. With data-kit-file-page you can drop anywhere on the page: while dragging, a veil appears with the given text. Drag the invoices or a folder here or choose from your computer XML or P7M, up to 2 MB each No file. When the files change the element receives kit:files with { files, items, rejected } : files are the accepted File s, items pairs them with the path ( { file, path } , useful for folders) and rejected lists the discarded ones with the reason ( type , size , count , folder ). You can also pass onFiles to Kit.file(element, options) . Option Attribute Default accept · multiple those of the <input> field any file, only one max data-kit-file-max (MB) no limit directory data-kit-file-dir or webkitdirectory folders not allowed – data-kit-file-page=\"text\" on the zone none: you only drop on the zone empty · button · clearLabe","data-kit-file-dir data-kit-file-page kit-dropzone data-kit-file data-kit-file-max kit-icon kit-mute Kit.file kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-file-empty"],["form-controls","Forms: select and file","combobox","Combobox","A text field with a list of suggestions that narrows as you type. Unlike the select you can also type a value that is not in the list. It needs kit.js . Up and down arrows move through the items, Enter chooses the highlighted one (on opening it is the first), Esc closes, Tab leaves. Choosing writes the value into the field and fires input and kit:change ( { value, label } ). Items are written in the HTML, as kit-opt inside a kit-pop ; the button with the arrow is added automatically. Tax regime RF01 Ordinary RF02 Minimum taxpayers RF19 Flat rate Value: – For a long list, or one computed from data, use Kit.combo . items is an array (or a function returning one) of strings or of { value, label, hint } objects. The filter searches label, note and value; if there are more than max items it shows max and invites you to keep typing. Customer (240 items, shows 8) Value: – Option Attribute Default items (JavaScript only) array, or a function that receives the typed text the kit-opt s already in the HTML max data-kit-combo-max 50 empty data-kit-combo-empty No results ( \"\" to show nothing) more data-kit-combo-more {n} more results: keep typing to narrow down filter – true ; with false the it","kit-opt kit-pop kit-field kit-combo data-kit-combo kit-input kit-opt-text Kit.combo kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-combo-max data-kit-combo-empty data-kit-combo-more"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","","Forms: layout and validation","Labels, help text, required fields, column, grid, horizontal and sectioned forms, valid and invalid states with messages, automatic validation, sizes, icons inside fields, field groups, floating labels, card-style checkboxes and the other controls.",""],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","labels","Labels, help and required fields","A field is a .kit-field : it can be a <label> wrapping the input (as on the Forms: basic fields page) or a <div> with a <label class=\"kit-label\" for=\"…\"> and the input next to it. The second form is needed when there are help text and messages below the field, and for the horizontal layout; it is also the one Django generates. .kit-hint is the help text, linked to the field with aria-describedby . .kit-required on the label adds the red asterisk; .kit-optional adds \"(optional)\", which you change with --kit-optional-text . The field's required attribute remains what counts for the browser and the server. Email We only write to you for the confirmation. Phone With the international prefix.","kit-field kit-label kit-hint kit-required kit-optional --kit-optional-text kit-fields kit-input"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","layout","Layout","",""],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","column","Column and grid",".kit-form puts the fields in a column with the kit's spacing ( --kit-sp ). For several fields on the same row there are two ways: .kit-fields (an adaptive grid, kit-field-wide takes two columns) or the 12-column grid with .kit-row and .kit-col-* , as in Bootstrap, to decide the width of each field and where they wrap. First name Last name Address City Country Italy France Spain Postal code","kit-form --kit-sp kit-fields kit-field-wide kit-row kit-col kit-col-12 kit-col-md-6 kit-field kit-label kit-input kit-col-6 kit-col-md-5 kit-col-md-4 kit-col-md-3"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","horizontal","Horizontal",".kit-form-h on the form (or .kit-field-h on a single field) puts the label on the left and the field, help and messages on the right. The label width is --kit-label-w ( 11rem ). Below 576 px the fields go back to a column. It needs the form with <div class=\"kit-field\"> and .kit-label . Company name VAT number 11 digits, without the IT prefix. Notes Cancel Save","kit-form-h kit-field-h --kit-label-w kit-field kit-label kit-form kit-input kit-hint kit-form-foot kit-form-foot-end kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","inline","Inline",".kit-form-inline aligns fields and buttons on one row that wraps by itself: for filters and searches. Search Status All Paid Unpaid Filter","kit-form-inline kit-field kit-label kit-input kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","sections","Sections and groups",".kit-form-section divides a long form into blocks, with a title and explanation on the left and the fields on the right (from 768 px; below that they stack). To group related fields, or radios, use <fieldset class=\"kit-fieldset\"> with the <legend> : a disabled on the fieldset disables the whole group. Profile How other users see you. Display name Bio One line about you. Notifications When to get an email. Notify me when an invoice arrives an invoice is due","kit-form-section kit-fieldset kit-form kit-form-section-title kit-form-section-desc kit-form-section-body kit-field kit-label kit-input kit-field-foot kit-hint kit-counter data-kit-count kit-check"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","states","States: valid, invalid, warning","is-valid , is-invalid and is-warning go on the field, or on its .kit-field , and apply to everything it contains: border, focus ring and, for groups, all the parts. aria-invalid=\"true\" counts as is-invalid (and is needed by screen readers). The message is a .kit-feedback with -valid , -invalid or -warning , which can be preceded by an icon. The states also work on select, combobox, file field, drop zone and date range. Customer code Code available. Email Enter a complete address. Price The price is zero. With the classes on a .kit-field the other parts react too, with no extra markup: Document type Choose… Invoice Credit note Choose a type. Period Enter the period. Terms I accept the terms of sale You must accept to continue. For a CSS-only check after the user has touched the field, class=\"kit-validate\" on the form uses :user-invalid : the border turns red (and with kit-validate-ok green) when the HTML rules are not met. It does not write messages: for those there is the validation below.","kit-field kit-feedback kit-fields kit-label kit-input kit-feedback-valid kit-icon kit-feedback-invalid kit-feedback-warning kit-select data-kit-select kit-select-btn kit-select-value kit-pop kit-opt kit-opt-text kit-daterange data-kit-daterange kit-check kit-validate kit-validate-ok"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","validation","Validation in the browser","data-kit-validate on a <form> (needs kit.js ) checks the fields with the HTML rules you already know ( required , type=\"email\" , pattern , min , max , minlength …): on submit it marks is-invalid , writes the message into the .kit-feedback-invalid (creating it if missing), links the message to the field with aria-describedby , moves focus to the first error and blocks submission, htmx included. A field turns red on blur only if the user typed in it, and the error disappears as soon as the value is correct. With data-kit-validate=\"ok\" the correct fields get is-valid . The messages are the browser's (in its language). To write your own: data-kit-msg on the field for any error, or data-kit-msg-required , -type , -pattern , -min , -max , -minlength , -maxlength , -step . It works with the kit's fields: calendar (its min , max and excluded-days rules), select, checkboxes and radios, file. Email Perfect. Password Delivery date I accept the terms Reset Send From JavaScript: Kit.validate(form) runs the same check and returns true or false (options { ok, focus } ); Kit.validate.reset(form) clears states and messages (the form's reset does it by itself too). If there are errors the form fires","data-kit-validate kit-feedback-invalid data-kit-msg data-kit-msg-required kit-form kit-field kit-label kit-required kit-input data-kit-msg-type kit-feedback kit-feedback-valid kit-control data-kit-msg-minlength kit-control-end data-kit-password kit-icon data-kit-datepicker data-kit-min kit-check kit-form-foot kit-btn kit-btn-primary Kit.validate"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","sizes","Sizes","kit-input-sm and kit-input-lg on a field; kit-field-sm|lg on a field with its buttons and selects; kit-form-sm|lg on the whole form; kit-input-group-sm|lg on a group. They change --kit-ctl (the height shared by fields and buttons), so they always stay at the same height. kit-btn-sm is the matching button. Search","kit-input-sm kit-input-lg kit-field-sm kit-form-sm kit-input-group-sm --kit-ctl kit-btn-sm kit-form kit-input kit-input-group kit-input-group-lg kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","icons","Icons inside fields",".kit-control wraps the field and leaves room for an icon on the left ( .kit-control-start ) and an icon or a button on the right ( .kit-control-end ): the field makes room by itself. With is-valid , is-invalid or is-warning on the .kit-control (or on its .kit-field ) the result icon appears on the right, drawn by CSS: a check, a cross or an exclamation mark, so with no images. data-kit-password on a button shows and hides the password ( aria-pressed and the text for screen readers change by themselves). Search Password User Email Incomplete address. Amount Check the amount.","kit-control kit-control-start kit-control-end kit-field data-kit-password kit-fields kit-label kit-icon kit-input kit-feedback kit-feedback-invalid kit-feedback-warning"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","groups","Field groups",".kit-input-group joins text ( .kit-input-text ), icons, fields and buttons into a single block with merged borders. It also works with a native select, a .kit-select , a combobox or a field with a calendar. The states ( is-invalid …) color all the parts. Amount € VAT excluded Website https:// .com Discount code Apply Price and currency EUR USD User @ No spaces.","kit-input-group kit-input-text kit-select kit-fields kit-field kit-field-wide kit-label kit-input kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-feedback kit-feedback-invalid"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","float","Floating label",".kit-float : the label sits inside the field and, when the field is filled or focused, rises and shrinks. CSS only. The field comes before the label and has placeholder=\" \" (a space). It works for input, textarea and select. It is not used on fields with the calendar. Full name Email Milan Turin Office Message","kit-float kit-fields kit-input kit-field-wide"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","check","Checkboxes, radios and cards",".kit-check works for checkboxes and radios. .kit-check-text adds a line of explanation below; .kit-check-group lays them out in a column and kit-check-inline in a row; .kit-check-card turns them into selectable cards ( .kit-check-cards puts them in a grid). Wrap the group in a fieldset with a legend . The is-invalid state marks the border of the radio or card. Delivery Standard 2–3 working days Express Next day, +€5 Pick-up in store Options Gift Invoice Insurance Plan Basic Up to 3 users Team Up to 20 users Company Unlimited users","kit-check kit-check-text kit-check-group kit-check-inline kit-check-card kit-check-cards kit-fields --kit-sp"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","controls","Other controls",".kit-input also applies to <textarea> (free height, resizable; kit-textarea-auto makes it grow with the text where the browser allows), to a native <select> (with the arrow drawn by CSS), to type=\"file\" and type=\"color\" . .kit-range is for type=\"range\" . readonly and disabled have a different background; .kit-input-plain shows a value as text, without a frame. data-kit-count=\"#id\" on a text element writes \"n / maxlength\" and turns yellow near the limit and red at the limit. Message At most 60 characters. Native select One Two Three File Color Quantity Read only Disabled As text jane@company.com","kit-input kit-textarea-auto kit-range kit-input-plain data-kit-count kit-fields kit-field kit-label kit-field-foot kit-hint kit-counter"],["form-layout","Forms: layout and validation","django","With Django","The class names are the ones Django writes in widgets; the error messages from form.errors go into a .kit-feedback-invalid . A filter or template tag, or a widget with attrs , puts the classes on the field. # forms.py class ContactForm(forms.Form): name = forms.CharField(widget=forms.TextInput(attrs={\"class\": \"kit-input\"})) email = forms.EmailField(widget=forms.EmailInput(attrs={\"class\": \"kit-input\"})) message = forms.CharField(max_length=300, widget=forms.Textarea(attrs={\"class\": \"kit-input\", \"rows\": 4})) <!-- _field.html: {% include \"_field.html\" with field=form.email %} --> <div class=\"kit-field{% if field.errors %} is-invalid{% endif %}\"> <label class=\"kit-label{% if field.field.required %} kit-required{% endif %}\" for=\"{{ field.id_for_label }}\">{{ field.label }}</label> {{ field }} {% if field.help_text %}<div class=\"kit-hint\">{{ field.help_text }}</div>{% endif %} {% for e in field.errors %}<div class=\"kit-feedback kit-feedback-invalid\">{{ e }}</div>{% endfor %} </div> The invalid field gets its border from the is-invalid class on the .kit-field ; to tell screen readers too that it is wrong, aria-invalid=\"true\" is added from the widget, or with data-kit-validate on the form k","kit-feedback-invalid kit-code data-kit-code kit-input kit-field kit-label kit-required kit-hint kit-feedback data-kit-validate"],["forms","Forms: basic fields","","Forms: basic fields","Text field, search, checkbox and switch. Buttons and fields have the same height ( --kit-ctl ), so they sit well on the same row.",""],["forms","Forms: basic fields","fields","Fields",".kit-field is the label with the field below it; .kit-input applies to <input> . .kit-fields lays out several fields in a grid that adapts. Name Date Amount Note A help text below the field. The rest of the forms is on these pages: Layout and validation (labels, help text, column, grid and horizontal forms, valid and invalid states with error messages, validation, sizes, icons inside fields, selectable groups and cards), Select and file (custom select, file field, drop zone, combobox) and Dates and times (optional calendar, designed for the phone too).","kit-field kit-input kit-fields kit-field-wide"],["forms","Forms: basic fields","search","Search","A field with a magnifier and a keyboard shortcut. It stretches to fill the row ( flex: 1 ). / Search","kit-bar kit-search kit-icon kit-input kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["forms","Forms: basic fields","checkbox","Checkbox and form footer","Hide duplicates Reset Apply","kit-form-foot kit-check kit-btn-group kit-btn kit-btn-primary"],["forms","Forms: basic fields","switch","Switch","An on/off that takes effect immediately, unlike a checkbox that is confirmed with a button. It is a normal <input type=\"checkbox\"> with role=\"switch\" : checked , disabled and the change event work as usual. kit-switch-between puts the text on the left and the switch at the far right. Hide duplicates Also show discarded Not available Notifications","kit-switch-between kit-stack kit-switch"],["grid","Grid","","Grid","A 12-column flexbox grid, with the same names as Bootstrap. It is built with rows and columns and changes as the screen width changes.",""],["grid","Grid","how-it-works","How it works","A .kit-row contains .kit-col-* columns; each row has 12 columns and wraps by itself. It is mobile first : a class without a breakpoint applies everywhere, kit-col-md-6 applies from 768px up. The row has negative margins that compensate the columns' padding (the gutters ): put it inside a container with padding, like .kit-main or .kit-card-body . The row's direct children are all columns: even a <div> without a class is 100% wide. Abbreviation From Example none 0px kit-col-6 sm 576px kit-col-sm-6 md 768px kit-col-md-6 lg 992px kit-col-lg-6 xl 1200px kit-col-xl-6","kit-row kit-col kit-col-md-6 kit-main kit-card-body kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-col-6 kit-col-sm-6 kit-col-lg-6 kit-col-xl-6"],["grid","Grid","columns","Columns","kit-col-N with N from 1 to 12: the column takes N twelfths of the row. kit-col-4 kit-col-4 kit-col-4 kit-col-8 kit-col-4","kit-col kit-stack kit-row kit-col-4 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center kit-col-8"],["grid","Grid","responsive","Responsive","Combine several classes: a full-width column on the phone, half from md , a quarter from xl . Resize the window to see them change. 12 → md 6 → xl 3 12 → md 6 → xl 3 12 → md 6 → xl 3 12 → md 6 → xl 3","kit-stack kit-row kit-col-12 kit-col-md-6 kit-col-xl-3 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center"],["grid","Grid","flexible","Flexible columns","kit-col splits the remaining space in equal parts; kit-col-auto is as wide as its content. kit-col kit-col-auto kit-col kit-col kit-col-6 kit-col","kit-col kit-col-auto kit-stack kit-row kit-card kit-card-body kit-center kit-col-6"],["grid","Grid","row-cols","Columns per row","On the row, kit-row-cols-N (N from 1 to 6) decides how many cells fit in a row, with no classes on the cells. It is the most convenient way for KPI cards. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8","kit-row-cols kit-stack kit-row kit-row-cols-2 kit-row-cols-md-4 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center"],["grid","Grid","offset-order","Offset and order","kit-offset-N moves the column right by N twelfths. kit-order-first , kit-order-last and kit-order-0…5 change the display order without touching the HTML. kit-col-md-6 kit-offset-md-3 1st in the code, last 2nd 3rd in the code, first","kit-offset kit-order-first kit-order-last kit-order-0 kit-stack kit-row kit-col-md-6 kit-offset-md-3 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center kit-col-4"],["grid","Grid","alignment","Alignment","On the row, kit-align-items-* aligns vertically and kit-justify-content-* horizontally. On a single column kit-align-self-* applies. align-items-center centered centered justify-content-center","kit-align-items kit-justify-content kit-align-self kit-stack kit-row kit-align-items-center kit-col-4 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center kit-py-4 kit-py-5 kit-justify-content-center"],["grid","Grid","gutter","Gutter","The space between columns is adjusted with kit-g-0…5 (horizontal and vertical), kit-gx-* and kit-gy-* . By default it is --kit-sp , so it tightens by itself on the phone; with kit-g-md-4 it changes from a breakpoint. kit-g-0 kit-g-0 kit-g-4 kit-g-4 kit-g-4 kit-g-4","kit-g-0 kit-gx kit-gy --kit-sp kit-g-md-4 kit-stack kit-row kit-col-6 kit-card kit-card-body kit-center kit-g-4"],["grid","Grid","nested","Nested rows","Inside a column you can put another row, with its own 12 columns. Remember the container's padding (here kit-card-body ). kit-col-md-8, with a row inside kit-col-6 kit-col-6 kit-col-md-4","kit-card-body kit-stack kit-row kit-col-md-8 kit-card kit-mute kit-col-6 kit-center kit-col-md-4"],["grid","Grid","equal-height","Cards of equal height","The columns of a row already have the same height, but the card inside does not. Add kit-h-100 to the card. A little text. Much more text, which runs over several lines and makes the column taller than the other: with kit-h-100 the two cards end at the same height.","kit-h-100 kit-stack kit-row kit-col-md-6 kit-card kit-card-body"],["grid","Grid","css-grid","Alternative: CSS Grid","When you do not need per-column breakpoints, kit-grid fills the row with as many columns as fit (at least 240px each). kit-grid-2 and kit-grid-3 fix 2 or 3 columns (just one below 900px). kit-grid 1 kit-grid 2 kit-grid 3 kit-grid 4","kit-grid kit-grid-2 kit-grid-3 kit-stack kit-card kit-card-body kit-center"],["grid","Grid","dashboard","Structure of a dashboard","The most common scheme: KPIs at the top, a chart with a side panel, then a full-width table. The complete result is in the sample dashboard . Documents 1,284 +4% Total €48,920 +1.2% To review 17 −3 Discarded 2 +1 Chart (kit-col-xl-8) Side panel (kit-col-xl-4) Table (kit-col-12)","kit-stack kit-row kit-row-cols-2 kit-row-cols-lg-4 kit-card kit-kpi kit-h-100 kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-badge-warning kit-badge-danger kit-col-12 kit-col-xl-8 kit-card-body kit-center kit-mute kit-py-5 kit-col-xl-4"],["icons","Icons","","Icons","The kit's icons: an SVG sprite you include with one line of JavaScript.",""],["icons","Icons","usage","Usage","Icons are strokes on a 24×24 grid that take the text color ( currentColor ). They are used with <svg class=\"kit-icon\"> and <use> ; the name is the symbol's id, preceded by i- . Download An icon on its own, without text, needs an aria-label on the button that contains it. If it is only decorative, add aria-hidden=\"true\" to the <svg> .","kit-icon kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-icon kit-btn-danger"],["icons","Icons","installation","Installation","Sprites cannot be loaded from another domain with a <use> that points to an SVG file: that is why the kit inserts them with a small script. Add it before closing </body> : <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/N1K1TAS95/dashboard-kit@v0.11.0/dist/kit-icons.js\" integrity=\"sha384-HrtxdGgc5dQOvkslXHapNsTNVhGGEfQ6FWYOn5zdFAIrc/6z/AbizR+W6xdilWS9\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script> If you prefer not to use JavaScript, copy the content of dist/kit-icons.svg to the start of the <body> (this is what this documentation does) or keep only the icons you need in the sprite. If you already have your own sprite with the same ids, the first one the browser finds wins: there is no conflict, but check that the icons are the ones you expect.","kit-code data-kit-code kit-icons kit-alert"],["icons","Icons","sizes","Size and color","The icon is 18px and takes the text color. To change it use width / height and color .","kit-icon --kit-success --kit-danger"],["icons","Icons","list","List","All the available icons, with the name to use after #i- . chev chev-up chev-left chev-right arrow-up arrow-down arrow-left arrow-right expand external plus minus check x search download upload refresh edit trash copy filter sliders menu more more-v home user bell calendar file folder eye sun text moon auto info ok warn error","kit-icon"],["icons","Icons","adding","Adding an icon","Icons are defined in tools/icons.py (name → SVG strokes). Add a line, then run python3 tools/icons.py : it regenerates dist/kit-icons.svg and dist/kit-icons.js . Draw them on 24×24, stroke only, with no fixed colors.","kit-icons"],["index","Introduction","","Introduction","Dashboard Kit is a small CSS framework, with optional JavaScript, for building dashboards. A single file, no dependencies, light and dark themes, and a 12-column grid like Bootstrap.",""],["index","Introduction","installation","Installation","From a CDN (jsDelivr), with the version pinned and the integrity attribute (SRI): if the file were tampered with, the browser rejects it. <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/N1K1TAS95/dashboard-kit@v0.11.0/dist/kit.css\" integrity=\"sha384-caI9z5CMWhN61so69TJdI2W0CNgg9S/+kpJOHLXAtH+BJfDxBaY1a+izk6JVhNZY\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"> <!-- optional: theme, select, tabs, dialog, menus, toasts --> <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/N1K1TAS95/dashboard-kit@v0.11.0/dist/kit.js\" integrity=\"sha384-E8k1BIsidNO7DKy6DTwVicqmImx7UzRaFtUix8pWXq17/+cZrNcEc7l3AbzfrSRd\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script> Or locally: copy dist/kit.css (and dist/kit.js ) into your project and link them with a relative path. If your site has a Content-Security-Policy, allow https://cdn.jsdelivr.net in style-src and script-src . Avoid @main or @latest : they are not pinned versions and jsDelivr caches them for hours. The texts kit.js writes by itself (button labels, \"No results\", the calendar…) follow <html lang> : English if missing, Italian with lang=\"it\" . See Languages .","kit-code data-kit-code kit-alert"],["index","Introduction","page-template","Page template","The minimal skeleton with a fixed header and a grid for the content. In the editor you get it by typing kit-page + Tab (see VS Code snippets ). <!doctype html> <html lang=\"en\"> <head> <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"> <meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"> <title>My dashboard</title> <script src=\"dist/kit.js\"></script> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"dist/kit.css\"> </head> <body> <header class=\"kit-header\"> <h1 class=\"kit-brand\">Name <span>app</span></h1> </header> <main class=\"kit-main\"> <div class=\"kit-container\"> <div class=\"kit-row\"> <div class=\"kit-col-12 kit-col-lg-8\"><section class=\"kit-card kit-card-body\">…</section></div> <div class=\"kit-col-12 kit-col-lg-4\"><section class=\"kit-card kit-card-body\">…</section></div> </div> </div> </main> </body> </html>","kit-page kit-code data-kit-code kit-header kit-brand kit-main kit-container kit-row kit-col-12 kit-col-lg-8 kit-card kit-card-body kit-col-lg-4"],["index","Introduction","icons","Icons","The kit does not include icons: .kit-icon only gives an <svg> its size and stroke. You use an inline sprite in the page and call it with <use> , so the icons take the text color. <svg width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"position:absolute\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><defs> <symbol id=\"i-search\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"7\"/><path d=\"m20 20-3.5-3.5\"/></symbol> </defs></svg> <button class=\"kit-btn\"><svg class=\"kit-icon\"><use href=\"#i-search\"/></svg>Search</button>","kit-icon kit-code data-kit-code kit-btn"],["index","Introduction","browsers","Supported browsers","The light/dark colors use light-dark() , so you need Chrome/Edge 123+, Safari 17.5+ or Firefox 120+. The rest (flexbox, grid, color-mix() , :has() only in the documentation pages) is supported by those same versions.",""],["index","Introduction","from-bootstrap","If you know Bootstrap","The grid, the utilities and the names follow Bootstrap, with the kit- prefix. The differences to keep in mind: Bootstrap Dashboard Kit Note .row , .col-md-6 .kit-row , .kit-col-md-6 Identical, but with default gutters equal to --kit-sp (they tighten on phones). .btn btn-primary .kit-btn kit-btn-primary Variants are separate classes, not double-dash modifiers. .d-flex , .mt-3 .kit-d-flex , .kit-mt-3 Spacing scale 0–5 in px: 0, 4, 8, 16, 24, 48. .modal , .dropdown <dialog class=\"kit-dialog\"> , .kit-dropdown The dialog is the browser's native element. Theme with data-bs-theme data-theme on <html> Automatic by default, can be forced to light or dark. xxl breakpoint — Not present: add it in tools/gen-grid.py .","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-row kit-col-md-6 --kit-sp kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-d-flex kit-mt-3 kit-dialog kit-dropdown"],["javascript","JavaScript","","JavaScript","JavaScript is optional. Without kit.js all the styling works; you only need it for the parts that move: theme, tabs, select, menus, dialogs and toasts.",""],["javascript","JavaScript","principles","Principles","No dependencies and no build step: a single file, dist/kit.js . It is activated with data-kit-* attributes, without writing code. It uses no innerHTML , eval or inline scripts: it works with script-src 'self' . Handlers are delegated to the document, so they also apply to HTML added after load.",""],["javascript","JavaScript","attributes","Attributes","Attribute Where What it does data-kit-theme-set=\"auto|light|dark\" a button or a menu item Sets the theme and remembers it. data-kit-fs-set=\"md|lg|xl\" a button or a menu item Sets the text size of the whole page and remembers it. data-kit-fs-step=\"1|-1\" a button Makes the text one step larger ( 1 ) or smaller ( -1 ); it disables itself at the ends. data-kit-reset a button Restores theme, text size and width (see the settings panel ). data-kit-layout-set=\"boxed|fluid\" a button Chooses centered or full-width content and remembers it. data-kit-layout-toggle a button Switches between the two widths. data-kit-nav=\"#id\" the button of a navbar Opens or closes the given collapsible menu ( .kit-navbar-menu ); Esc or a click outside closes it. data-kit-toggle=\"#id\" a button Opens or closes the given .kit-pop . data-kit-select .kit-select Turns the list of options into a select. On a native <select> it replaces it with the kit's menu ( details ). data-kit-tabs .kit-tabs Activates the tabs; each .kit-tab has data-kit-panel=\"#id\" . data-kit-open=\"#id\" a button Opens the given <dialog> . data-kit-confirm=\"Question?\" a button, a link or a <form> First asks for confirmation in a dialog; the action ","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-theme-set data-kit-fs-set data-kit-fs-step data-kit-reset data-kit-layout-set data-kit-layout-toggle data-kit-nav kit-navbar-menu data-kit-toggle kit-pop data-kit-select kit-select data-kit-tabs kit-tabs kit-tab data-kit-panel data-kit-open data-kit-confirm data-kit-sort data-kit-filter data-kit-page data-kit-datepicker data-kit-timepicker data-kit-daterange data-kit-validate data-kit-password data-kit-count data-kit-close"],["javascript","JavaScript","api","API","Kit.toast(\"Saved!\"); // temporary message; options: type, title, duration, position, action, progress (see Dialogs and menus) Kit.toast.clear(); // closes all toasts await Kit.confirm(\"Delete?\", { danger: true }); // confirmation dialog → true / false (options: text, confirm, cancel, danger, type) Kit.undo(\"Deleted\", { onUndo, onCommit }); // the action happens now, with an \"Undo\" toast; onCommit if it is not undone Kit.theme.get(); // \"auto\" | \"light\" | \"dark\" Kit.theme.set(\"dark\"); // sets and saves the theme Kit.fontSize.get(); // \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\" | \"xl\" Kit.fontSize.set(\"lg\"); // sets and saves the text size Kit.fontSize.step(1); // one step larger (-1: smaller) Kit.reset(); // restores theme, text and width Kit.layout.get(); // \"boxed\" | \"fluid\" Kit.layout.set(\"fluid\"); // full-width content (remembered) Kit.layout.toggle(); // switches Kit.table(\"#table\", { sort: true, size: 10 }); // sorting, filter and pages of a table (see Tables); Kit.paginate(\"#table\", 10) for pages only Kit.datepicker(\"#due\"); // calendar on a date, date-time or time field (see Dates and times); Kit.daterange(\"#period\") for the range Kit.validate(\"#form\"); // checks a form (true/false) and marks its f","kit-code data-kit-code Kit.toast Kit.confirm Kit.undo Kit.theme Kit.fontSize Kit.reset Kit.layout Kit.table Kit.paginate Kit.datepicker Kit.daterange Kit.validate Kit.date Kit.i Kit.init kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary data-kit-theme-set"],["javascript","JavaScript","languages","Languages","The texts kit.js writes by itself (the \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" buttons, labels for screen readers, \"No results\", table pages, the calendar) come from a dictionary per language. English (the base language) and Italian are built in. The language is the one in <html lang=\"…\"> : without the attribute English is used, so on an Italian page remember to write <html lang=\"it\"> . With a language that has a region ( pt-BR ) it looks for that first, then the language without the region ( pt ), then English: a dictionary can contain only what changes. Attributes and options ( data-kit-empty , Kit.confirm(…, { cancel }) ) always win over the dictionary. The calendar and the tables follow the language too: the date order ( mm/dd/yyyy in English, dd/mm/yyyy in Italian), the first day of the week (Sunday in English, Monday in Italian), month and day names, and the decimal separator used to sort the numbers in a column ( 1,250.50 or 1.250,50 ). The submitted value is always ISO. Kit.i18n.lang(); // \"en\": the language in use (from <html lang>) Kit.i18n.lang(\"de\"); // sets it by hand, ignoring <html lang>; Kit.i18n.lang(\"\") goes back to <html lang> // Another language: just write what you need, the re","data-kit-empty Kit.confirm kit-code data-kit-code Kit.i"],["javascript","JavaScript","events","Events","They are CustomEvent s that bubble up the DOM: listen on the document or on the element. Event On detail kit:change .kit-select { value } : the chosen data-value (for a native select also label ) kit:sort , kit:filter , kit:page <table> { column, direction } , { query, count } , { page, pages, size, total } kit:change date, time or range field { value, display } (ISO and the field's text) or { from, to } kit:invalid <form data-kit-validate> { fields } : the fields that are invalid at submit time kit:tab .kit-tabs { tab } : the activated tab element kit:theme <html> the theme that was set kit:fs <html> the text size that was set ( sm , md , lg or xl ) kit:reset <html> the settings were restored kit:layout <html> the width that was set ( boxed or fluid ) document.addEventListener(\"kit:change\", (e) => { console.log(\"Chosen:\", e.detail.value); });","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-select data-kit-validate kit-tabs kit-code data-kit-code"],["javascript","JavaScript","keyboard","Keyboard","Open menus and selects : up/down arrows to move through the items, Enter or Space to choose, Esc to close (focus returns to the button). Tabs : left/right arrows move to the neighboring tab. Dialog : Esc closes it (native behavior); so does a click on the backdrop.",""],["layout","Layout","","Layout","Container, fixed header, element bars, stacking and side panel: the structure of a page. For columns see the grid .",""],["layout","Layout","structure","Page structure","A page is a fixed .kit-header at the top and a .kit-main containing a .kit-container . Inside the container you use the grid or .kit-stack . <header class=\"kit-header\"> <h1 class=\"kit-brand\">Name <span>app</span></h1> <span class=\"kit-spacer\"></span> <!-- buttons, menus, theme… --> </header> <main class=\"kit-main\"> <div class=\"kit-container kit-stack\"> … </div> </main> .kit-header : --kit-hh tall, stays stuck to the top (sticky). Table headers stick right below it. .kit-brand : a title whose second word, in a <span> , is colored with the accent. .kit-main : 24px of inner margin (16px below 900px) and 80px at the bottom. .kit-container : centered content, at most --kit-container-w (1200px) wide. See Content width .","kit-header kit-main kit-container kit-stack kit-code data-kit-code kit-brand kit-spacer --kit-hh --kit-container-w"],["layout","Layout","content-width","Content width","Narrow, centered content reads better for texts and forms; a dashboard with tables and charts often does better at full width. The kit allows both, at two levels. Class Behavior kit-container Centered, at most --kit-container-w wide. It follows the global switch (below): with data-layout=\"fluid\" it fills the whole window. kit-container-boxed Always centered, whatever the switch. kit-container-fluid Always full width. Global switch Put data-layout=\"boxed\" or \"fluid\" on <html> to choose the width of the whole page ( boxed by default). With kit.js the user can change it from a button and the choice is remembered, like the theme. The width only changes when the window is wider than --kit-container-w . <!-- full-width content by default --> <html lang=\"en\" data-layout=\"fluid\"> <!-- a button that lets the user choose (it is remembered) --> <button class=\"kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon\" data-kit-layout-toggle aria-label=\"Full-width content\">…</button> Kit.layout.set(\"fluid\"); // or \"boxed\"; Kit.layout.toggle() switches These documentation pages use kit-container-boxed and always stay centered. To see the switch in action open the sample dashboard : it starts at full width and has the ","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-container --kit-container-w kit-container-boxed kit-container-fluid kit-code data-kit-code kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon data-kit-layout-toggle Kit.layout kit-alert kit-header kit-brand kit-spacer"],["layout","Layout","stack","Stacking: kit-stack","It lays out its children in a column with a constant gap ( --kit-sp ). It is the simplest way to put cards one under the other. First card Second card Third card","--kit-sp kit-stack kit-card kit-card-body"],["layout","Layout","bar","Element bar: kit-bar","Elements side by side and vertically centered, wrapping when there is no room: toolbars, filters, groups of buttons. .kit-spacer pushes what follows to the right. New Import Settings kit-bar is not the grid's row: for columns use kit-row .","kit-spacer kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost kit-alert kit-row"],["layout","Layout","split","Side panel: kit-split","A list with, next to it, a detail panel that opens when a row is selected. Above 900px the panel sits next to the list and stays put while the list scrolls. Below 900px it covers the page from the right, with a dark veil behind it, and a click on the veil closes it. With kit-split-lg instead of kit-split the switch happens below 1250px, for lists that need a lot of room. With kit.js three attributes are enough: data-kit-split-open=\"#id\" on whatever opens it (a row, a button), data-kit-split-close and data-kit-split-full inside the panel. The second closes, the third toggles between \"next to the list\" and \"full width\" (the list disappears). With data-kit-split on the container Esc closes the panel, or brings it back next to the list if it was full width. On opening, focus goes to the panel and on closing it returns to whatever opened it. Invoice Customer Amount 2026/014 Smith Ltd €1,240.00 2026/015 Brown Inc €860.50 2026/016 Green Services €3,075.00 Invoice 2026/014 Smith Ltd Date 03/12/2026 Taxable amount €1,016.39 VAT 22% €223.61 Total €1,240.00 The panel is made of kit-split-head (title in kit-split-title and buttons) and kit-split-body , which is the part that scrolls. Width nex","kit-split-lg kit-split data-kit-split-open data-kit-split-close data-kit-split-full data-kit-split kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-table-hover kit-right kit-num kit-split-panel kit-split-head kit-split-title kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-icon kit-split-body kit-kv --kit-split-w --kit-split-overlay-w Kit.split"],["layout","Layout","spacing","Base spacing","Three tokens govern the interface's breathing room (see Themes and tokens ): --kit-sp (margins, distance between cards, inner padding, gutter), --kit-rad (corners) and --kit-ctl (height of buttons and fields). Below 760px --kit-sp goes down from 16 to 8px.","--kit-sp --kit-rad --kit-ctl"],["navbar","Navbar","","Navbar","The top bar with logo, items, dropdown menus, actions and a collapsible menu on small screens.",""],["navbar","Navbar","base","Basic navbar","The navbar is a .kit-header with the kit-navbar class. Inside go, in this order, the logo ( kit-brand ), the menu ( kit-navbar-menu ) with the list of items ( kit-nav ) and, if needed, actions on the right, and finally the button that opens the menu on small screens ( kit-navbar-toggler ). With kit-navbar-expand-md the menu is inline from 768px up and, below that, it hides behind the three-line button. Try narrowing the window. The button has data-kit-nav with the menu's id: kit.js is needed. Invoices app Home Documents Customers Archive New","kit-header kit-navbar kit-brand kit-navbar-menu kit-nav kit-navbar-toggler kit-navbar-expand-md data-kit-nav kit-nav-link kit-spacer kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-icon"],["navbar","Navbar","items","Items","kit-nav-link is used on an <a> (or on a <button> ). The current page is marked with aria-current=\"page\" (or with the is-active class): besides the color, screen readers read it too. To disable an item there is aria-disabled=\"true\" or the disabled attribute. Inside the item you can put an icon or a kit-badge . Home Messages 3 Disabled","kit-nav-link kit-badge kit-nav kit-icon kit-badge-danger"],["navbar","Navbar","dropdown","Items with a dropdown menu","An item can open a menu: it is the same dropdown menu as for buttons ( kit-dropdown , kit-pop , kit-opt ), placed inside an <li> . The up and down arrows move through the items, Enter selects, Esc closes. In the collapsible menu the dropdowns open inline, below the item. Invoices app Home Documents Invoices Received Issued Credit notes Report By year By supplier","kit-dropdown kit-pop kit-opt kit-header kit-navbar kit-navbar-expand-md kit-brand kit-navbar-menu kit-nav kit-nav-link data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop-group kit-pop-sep kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-navbar-toggler data-kit-nav"],["navbar","Navbar","actions","Search, theme and actions","After kit-spacer goes what sits on the right: a search field, the settings panel, a user menu. What you put inside kit-navbar-menu hides with the menu. What you put in kit-navbar-actions , after the menu and before the button, always stays visible: it is the right place for theme and user. Invoices app Home Documents Customers Profile Sign out The order in the code matters: logo, menu, kit-navbar-actions , button. The collapsible menu is out of the flow, so on a small screen only the logo, actions and button remain on the bar.","kit-spacer kit-navbar-menu kit-navbar-actions kit-header kit-navbar kit-navbar-expand-lg kit-brand kit-nav kit-nav-link kit-input kit-dropdown kit-btn kit-btn-icon kit-btn-ghost data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop kit-pop-right kit-opt kit-opt-danger kit-navbar-toggler data-kit-nav kit-alert"],["navbar","Navbar","breakpoint","When it opens inline","Class Inline from kit-navbar-expand-sm 576px kit-navbar-expand-md 768px kit-navbar-expand-lg 992px kit-navbar-expand-xl 1200px none never: the button is always there They are the same breakpoints as the grid . With too many items pick a higher one: if the items do not fit, they wrap or overflow the bar.","kit-table kit-navbar-expand-sm kit-navbar-expand-md kit-navbar-expand-lg kit-navbar-expand-xl"],["navbar","Navbar","collapsible","Collapsible menu","On a small screen the menu drops below the bar, full width, and scrolls if it is taller than the window. Below, the navbar without kit-navbar-expand-* , so the button is always there. Invoices app Home Documents Received Issued Customers It closes with a second click on the button, with Esc (focus returns to the button), by clicking outside the bar or by choosing a link in the menu. If the window widens past the breakpoint, the \"open\" state is reset. The button has aria-expanded and aria-controls , updated by kit.js .","kit-navbar-expand kit-header kit-navbar kit-brand kit-navbar-menu kit-nav kit-nav-link kit-dropdown data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop kit-opt kit-input kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-navbar-toggler data-kit-nav"],["navbar","Navbar","container","Aligned with the content: kit-container","As with the normal header, put a container inside the navbar: the bar stays as wide as the window (with the background and border), but logo, items and actions align with the page content. The container becomes the navbar's inner row. The collapsible menu stays as wide as the window. Class Effect on the navbar kit-container Centered, with maximum width --kit-container-w . It follows the global switch data-layout=\"boxed|fluid\" : with fluid it fills the whole window, like the content. kit-container-boxed Always centered, whatever the switch. kit-container-fluid Always full width. none The whole window, with only the header's side margin. In the examples the maximum width is reduced to 36rem, just to show the difference; the dashed box is the container. The first is kit-container-boxed , the second kit-container-fluid . Boxed Home Documents New Fluid Home Documents New The container goes inside the navbar and the page content ( .kit-main ) uses the same one: this way navbar and page stay aligned, even when the user changes width from the settings . The collapsible menu ( kit-navbar-menu ) is positioned relative to the navbar, not to the container: that is why it stays full width.","kit-table kit-container --kit-container-w kit-container-boxed kit-container-fluid kit-header kit-navbar kit-navbar-expand-md kit-brand kit-navbar-menu kit-nav kit-nav-link kit-spacer kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-navbar-toggler data-kit-nav kit-icon kit-main kit-alert"],["navbar","Navbar","vertical","Vertical list","kit-nav-col lays the items out in a column: for a side menu, or for a list of sections. Overview Documents Settings","kit-nav-col kit-nav kit-nav-link"],["navbar","Navbar","accessibility","Accessibility","Put the list inside a <nav> with aria-label (if there is more than one on the page). Items are real links and buttons: they can be reached with Tab and have a focus ring. The menu button has an aria-label , because it contains only an icon.",""],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","","Tabs and breadcrumb","Tabs, segmented control, pills, chips and breadcrumb: ways to choose what to show, to filter and to find your way.",""],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","tab","Tabs","With data-kit-tabs and kit.js the tabs show the panel indicated by data-kit-panel and move with the arrow keys. Inside the tab bar you can put kit-spacer and some buttons on the right. Documents Customers Export Documents content. Customers content.","data-kit-tabs data-kit-panel kit-spacer kit-tabs kit-tab kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-icon kit-card kit-card-body kit-tabpanel"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","segmented","Segmented control","A few exclusive options, to change view or filter. The active option has is-on (or aria-pressed=\"true\" ): activating it is your code's job. All Received Issued","kit-seg"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","pill","Pill","Selectable filters, optionally with a counter in <small> . 2026 124 2025 98 2024 71","kit-bar kit-pill"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","chip","Chip","Active filters, removable with a click. Here the example really removes them. Year 2026 × Amount > €100 ×","kit-bar kit-chip"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","breadcrumb","Breadcrumb","It shows where you are in the site hierarchy and lets you go back up. It is CSS only: a <nav class=\"kit-breadcrumb\"> with an <ol> , one <li> per level and aria-current=\"page\" on the last one, which is the current page and not a link. The separator is drawn by CSS, so the screen reader reads only the names. The <nav> needs an aria-label (for example \"Breadcrumb\") to tell it apart from the others. Home Invoices 2026 FT-0042","kit-breadcrumb"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","breadcrumb-variants","Separator and icon","By default the separator is a small arrow; kit-breadcrumb-slash uses the slash. An icon ( kit-icon ) before an item's text aligns by itself: usually the house for the first one. Home Customers Alpha Services Ltd","kit-breadcrumb-slash kit-icon kit-breadcrumb"],["navigation","Tabs and breadcrumb","breadcrumb-collapse","Long paths on narrow screens","With kit-breadcrumb-collapse , below 576px only the first and last items remain, on a single line (the last one is shortened with an ellipsis if it does not fit). In place of the hidden items a kit-breadcrumb-more item with \"…\" appears, which you write after the first one and which is only visible on those screens; it is aria-hidden because the hidden items are not read. Narrow the window to see it. Home … Accounting Sales invoices 2026 FT-0042 · Alpha Services Ltd With a kit-header or at the top of a page the breadcrumb sits well above the title, with a margin-bottom of one or two spacing units. If the server computes the levels (Django, for example) a loop is enough that writes an <li> with a link for each ancestor and the last one with aria-current .","kit-breadcrumb-collapse kit-breadcrumb-more kit-breadcrumb kit-header"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","","Dialogs and menus","Dialog windows, pop-up menus and temporary messages. They require kit.js .",""],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","dialog","Dialog","It uses the native <dialog> element: the browser handles focus, the Esc key and the darkened backdrop. The kit adds the style and two attributes: data-kit-open to open it, data-kit-close to close it. A click on the backdrop closes it. The dialog is a card overlay: it has the same three parts ( kit-card-head , kit-card-body , kit-card-foot ), the same padding and the same border. If the content is tall, only the body scrolls; title and buttons stay visible. This also holds if the three parts are inside a <form> ( <form method=\"dialog\"> ). If instead the content is placed directly in the dialog, without kit-card-body , the whole dialog scrolls. The width is chosen with a class: kit-dialog-sm (340px), no class (440px), kit-dialog-lg (700px, also kit-dialog-wide ), kit-dialog-xl (960px) and kit-dialog-full (the whole window minus the margins). For your own value set --kit-dialog-w : on a single dialog ( style=\"--kit-dialog-w: 520px\" ) or on all of them ( :root { --kit-dialog-w: 520px } ). On narrow screens the dialog never goes outside the window. Small Wide Extra wide Custom 520px kit-dialog-sm 340px. Close kit-dialog-lg 700px. Close kit-dialog-xl 960px. Close --kit-dialog-w: 520px Cu","data-kit-open data-kit-close kit-card-head kit-card-body kit-card-foot kit-dialog-sm kit-dialog-lg kit-dialog-wide kit-dialog-xl kit-dialog-full --kit-dialog-w kit-btn kit-dialog kit-btn-primary kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-icon kit-mute kit-field kit-input"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","drawer","Drawer","A dialog that slides in from an edge of the window: for a detail, an advanced filter or a long form, when you want to keep the page in view. It is the same <dialog> , with the same parts, the same attributes ( data-kit-open , data-kit-close ) and the same Esc, backdrop click and focus; you only add the kit-drawer class. By default it comes from the right; kit-drawer-left , kit-drawer-top and kit-drawer-bottom change the side. On a narrow screen it takes the full width. From the right From the left From the bottom Filters Customer From To Cancel Apply Menu A narrow drawer from the left: kit-drawer-left kit-drawer-sm . Summary From the bottom, at most --kit-drawer-h tall (40% of the window). The width is --kit-drawer-w (420px), or a class: kit-drawer-sm (320px), kit-drawer-lg (640px), kit-drawer-xl (860px). For top and bottom drawers the maximum height is --kit-drawer-h . The animation (0.25 s) is turned off by prefers-reduced-motion and, like the dialog's, requires a recent browser. If the detail has to stay next to a list rather than overlay it, use the side panel .","data-kit-open data-kit-close kit-drawer kit-drawer-left kit-drawer-top kit-drawer-bottom kit-btn kit-dialog kit-card-head kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-icon kit-card-body kit-stack kit-field kit-input kit-card-foot kit-btn-primary kit-drawer-sm kit-mute --kit-drawer-h --kit-drawer-w kit-drawer-lg kit-drawer-xl"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","confirm","Asking for confirmation","A dialog with \"Confirm\" and \"Cancel\" interrupts whoever is working, and if it appears too often people learn to press \"Confirm\" without reading. It is better to choose based on how serious the mistake would be. If the action… Use can be undone (archiving, moving, deleting with a trash) Undo : the action runs immediately and the toast offers \"Undo\" cannot be undone (deleting forever, sending, paying) Confirm with Kit.confirm or data-kit-confirm is very serious or concerns a lot of data (deleting an archive) Confirm by typing the name In any case: write the precise verb on the confirm button (\"Delete 12 invoices\", not \"OK\"), and say in the text what happens.","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table Kit.confirm data-kit-confirm"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","confirm-js","Kit.confirm","Kit.confirm(question, options) opens the dialog by itself, without HTML, and returns a promise: true if the user confirms, false with \"Cancel\", Esc or a click on the backdrop. With danger: true the button is red and focus starts on \"Cancel\", so an absent-minded Enter does no harm; without it, focus is on \"Confirm\". Simple confirmation Dangerous action Option Values Default 1st argument the question (dialog title) Confirm the action? text explanation under the question none confirm · cancel text of the two buttons Confirm · Cancel danger true : red button, warning icon, focus on \"Cancel\" false type text to type to enable the confirmation none The text is always plain text, never HTML: you can also pass a name entered by the user. The dialog is a <dialog> with role=\"alertdialog\" : Tab stays inside, Esc cancels and on closing focus returns to the button that opened it.","Kit.confirm kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-danger kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-alert"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","confirm-name","Typing the name","For truly irreversible actions, type asks to write a text (usually the name of what is being deleted): until it matches, \"Confirm\" stays disabled. Case matters; spaces at the edges do not. Enter in the field confirms, if the text is right. Delete the archive…","kit-bar Kit.confirm kit-btn kit-btn-danger"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","confirm-attribute","Without JavaScript: data-kit-confirm","Put data-kit-confirm=\"Question?\" on a button, a link or a <form> : the click (or the form submit) opens the dialog and, only if the user confirms, the action proceeds as if nothing had been in between. The confirmation runs before your click handlers, which only fire after the \"yes\". The other options are attributes: data-kit-confirm-text , -ok , -cancel , -danger (no value) and -type . Delete invoice Send","data-kit-confirm data-kit-confirm-text kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-danger data-kit-confirm-ok data-kit-confirm-danger"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","undo","Undo instead of asking","For actions that can be undone, asking first is the worst choice: it slows everyone down to protect a few. Kit.undo does the opposite: the interface changes immediately and a toast with a time bar offers \"Undo\". When the time runs out (or the toast closes, or the page is left) onCommit runs, the real and final action; with \"Undo\" onUndo runs and onCommit never does. Invoice 2026/014 · Smith Ltd Delete The invoice is gone: now look at the toast. Options: onUndo , onCommit , duration (default 6000 ms), label (default \"Undo\"), type and position as in toasts . It returns { undo(), commit() } to decide from code. If onCommit has to reach a server, remember that when the page closes the browser may interrupt the request: use fetch with keepalive: true .","Kit.undo kit-bar kit-spacer kit-btn kit-btn-danger kit-mute"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","dialog-animation","Animation","All kit-dialog s appear and disappear with a short fade (0.18 s), a slight upward slide and the backdrop darkening. It turns itself off with prefers-reduced-motion . A recent browser is needed (Chrome 117, Safari 17.4, Firefox 129): in the others the dialog appears and disappears without animation, but works just the same.","kit-dialog"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu","Pop-up menu",".kit-pop is a panel that can be used on its own, for any menu: a row's actions, a button's items, the theme selector. A button with data-kit-toggle=\"#id\" opens the indicated .kit-pop (inside a .kit-dropdown , which positions it under the button). It closes with Esc, by clicking outside or by choosing an item; the arrow keys move through the items, Enter activates them. Actions Export CSV All the filtered rows Search documents","kit-pop data-kit-toggle kit-dropdown kit-btn kit-icon kit-opt kit-opt-text"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu-items","Items: buttons, links, separators","A .kit-opt item can be a <div> , a <button> or an <a> : use the button for an action and the link to change page. kit-opt-danger colors destructive actions, kit-pop-sep separates groups, kit-pop-group titles them and aria-disabled=\"true\" disables an item. Invoice Document Copy number Open in a page Download PDF Not available Delete","kit-opt kit-opt-danger kit-pop-sep kit-pop-group kit-dropdown kit-btn data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop kit-opt-text"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu-icon","Icon-only button","The classic \"more actions\" menu of a row. With kit-pop-right the panel aligns to the button's right edge, so it does not go off the page. Invoice 2026/0142 Edit Duplicate Delete","kit-pop-right kit-bar kit-dropdown kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop kit-opt kit-opt-text kit-pop-sep kit-opt-danger"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu-split","Split button","The main action on the left, the arrow with the alternatives on the right. kit-btn-split joins the two buttons. Export CSV Export Excel Export PDF","kit-btn-split kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-icon kit-dropdown kit-btn-icon data-kit-toggle kit-pop kit-pop-right kit-opt kit-opt-text"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu-up","Upwards","Near the bottom edge of the page add kit-pop-up : the panel opens above the button. Sort by Date Amount Supplier","kit-pop-up kit-dropdown kit-btn data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-pop kit-opt kit-opt-text"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","menu-static","Always visible","Without a button and without hidden , with kit-pop-static , the panel stays in the page flow: it is for a side menu or a list of actions. The items are normal buttons or links, so they can be reached with Tab. Account Profile Settings Sign out","kit-pop-static kit-pop kit-pop-group kit-opt kit-icon kit-opt-text kit-pop-sep kit-opt-danger"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","tooltip","Tooltip","A short hint on any element, with CSS only: the data-kit-tip attribute is enough. It appears on mouse hover (after a short wait) and on keyboard focus; with kit.js the Esc key hides it. The mouse can reach the tooltip without it disappearing. Received A link","data-kit-tip kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-icon kit-icon kit-badge kit-badge-warning"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","tooltip-position","Position","data-kit-tip-pos chooses the side: top (default), bottom , left , right . Top Bottom Left Right The tooltip is not a way to provide a label: an icon-only button must still have aria-label . Do not put essential information, links or buttons in it, because on touch and for screen reader users it may not appear. A disabled button does not receive the mouse: put the tooltip on a <span> that contains it. A container with hidden or scrolling overflow (for example .kit-table-wrap ) clips the tooltip: in that case choose a side that stays inside the container.","data-kit-tip-pos --kit-sp kit-bar kit-btn data-kit-tip kit-alert kit-alert-warning kit-table-wrap"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","toast","Toast","A short message that appears at the bottom and disappears by itself. It is shown from JavaScript with Kit.toast(\"text\") ; several toasts stack, up to six at a time. The neutral toast is inverted relative to the theme (dark on light, light on dark), so it always stands out from the content; colored ones fill the whole background. Show a toast","Kit.toast kit-btn"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","toast-types","Types, title and icon","The type option ( info , success , warning , danger ) colors the whole toast and adds the icon, if the page has the icons sprite ( kit-icons.js ); title adds a title. warning and danger toasts are announced immediately by screen readers ( role=\"alert\" ), the others discreetly. Info Success Warning Error","kit-icons kit-bar Kit.toast kit-btn"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","toast-action","Action and closing","With action the toast has a button (typically \"Undo\") and stays visible until you use it or close it with the × . duration is in milliseconds (default 4000); with 0 the toast does not disappear by itself. A bar at the bottom of the toast shows how long is left before closing (remove it with progress: false ). The time stops while the mouse or focus is on the toast, and the bar goes back to full: when you leave, the countdown restarts from the beginning. Kit.toast returns an object with close() to close it from code, and Kit.toast.clear() closes them all. With an action Stays until you close it Close all","Kit.toast kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-ghost"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","toast-position","Position","position chooses where it appears: bottom (default), top , bottom-start , bottom-end , top-start , top-end . The corners are the most used in dashboards, because they do not cover the central content. Top Top right Bottom right Bottom left Option Values Default type info · success · warning · danger neutral title text no title duration milliseconds; 0 = does not disappear 4000 position see above bottom action { label, onClick } none progress true · false true (remaining-time bar, if duration > 0) closable true · false true with an action or duration: 0 The toast text is always plain text: Kit.toast never interprets HTML, so you can also pass a value entered by the user.","kit-bar Kit.toast kit-btn kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-alert"],["overlays","Dialogs and menus","settings","Settings panel","A single menu for the user's preferences: theme (automatic, light, dark), text size and content width , plus \"Reset\". It is a pop-up menu with the kit-settings class, made of kit-seg groups whose buttons use the kit.js attributes you already know ( data-kit-theme-set , data-kit-fs-set , data-kit-layout-set ). Unlike a normal menu it stays open after each choice, so you can change several things in a row; it closes with Esc or by clicking outside. All choices are remembered. The rows are independent: remove the ones you do not need. data-kit-reset (or Kit.reset() ) brings everything back to the starting value: system theme, normal text, the width written in the HTML. It is the \"Settings\" menu at the top right of these pages. Settings Theme Auto Light Dark Text size A A A Content width Centered Full page Noticeable on screens wider than the content. Reset","kit-settings kit-seg data-kit-theme-set data-kit-fs-set data-kit-layout-set data-kit-reset Kit.reset kit-dropdown kit-btn data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-d-none kit-d-sm-inline kit-pop kit-pop-right kit-settings-row kit-settings-label kit-settings-foot kit-btn-ghost"],["sidebar","Sidebar","","Sidebar","The navigation bar on the left, with header, items, sub-items, account and utilities at the bottom. Slide-in on small screens, compact (icons only) on large ones.",""],["sidebar","Sidebar","base","Structure","The sidebar sits inside .kit-app , next to .kit-app-main : on the left the full-height bar, on the right the column with the header ( .kit-header ) and the content ( .kit-main ). The bar has three parts: kit-sidebar-head (logo), kit-sidebar-body (the items, scrolls by itself if there are many) and kit-sidebar-foot (account and utilities, always at the bottom). Invoices app Overview Alerts 3 Documents Invoices Due dates Archive MS Maria Smith maria@example.com Overview The page content. Each item is kit-side-link on an <a> or a <button> : icon, then the text inside <span class=\"kit-side-text\"> (needed, because it disappears in the compact version), then an optional badge. The current page is marked with aria-current=\"page\" (or is-active ); an unavailable item with aria-disabled=\"true\" . kit-side-title is the title of a group of items; in the compact version it becomes a separator line. Give the <aside> an id and an aria-label .","kit-app kit-app-main kit-header kit-main kit-sidebar-head kit-sidebar-body kit-sidebar-foot kit-sidebar kit-brand kit-icon kit-side-text kit-side-nav kit-side-link kit-badge kit-badge-danger kit-side-title kit-side-user kit-side-avatar kit-side-user-text kit-fs-4 kit-m-0 kit-mute"],["sidebar","Sidebar","header","Together with the header","The header is the usual one ( kit-header ), but it sits inside kit-app-main , above the content. The button that opens the sidebar lives there: data-kit-sidebar-toggle with, if needed, the bar's selector. The logo sits at the top of the sidebar, with the same height as the header ( --kit-hh ), so the two separator lines meet. <div class=\"kit-app kit-app-expand-lg\"> <aside class=\"kit-sidebar\" id=\"sidebar\" aria-label=\"Main\"> … </aside> <div class=\"kit-app-main\"> <header class=\"kit-header\"> <button class=\"kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon\" data-kit-sidebar-toggle=\"#sidebar\" aria-controls=\"sidebar\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Side menu\"> <svg class=\"kit-icon\"><use href=\"#i-menu\"/></svg> </button> … </header> <main class=\"kit-main\"> … </main> </div> </div> A complete example, to try by resizing the window: dashboard with sidebar .","kit-header kit-app-main data-kit-sidebar-toggle --kit-hh kit-code data-kit-code kit-app kit-app-expand-lg kit-sidebar kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-icon kit-main"],["sidebar","Sidebar","breakpoint","When it stays inline","Class on kit-app Inline from kit-app-expand-md 768px kit-app-expand-lg 992px kit-app-expand-xl 1200px none never: it is always slide-in Below that point the sidebar leaves the flow and sits off screen; the data-kit-sidebar-toggle button slides it in from the left, with the background darkening. It behaves like a dialog: the rest of the page cannot be reached ( inert ), focus moves to the bar, and it closes with Esc , with a click on the background or by choosing a link, returning focus to the button. If the window widens past the breakpoint, the \"open\" state is reset.","kit-table kit-app kit-app-expand-md kit-app-expand-lg kit-app-expand-xl data-kit-sidebar-toggle"],["sidebar","Sidebar","compact","Compact, icons only","On large screens the same button compresses the bar into a column of icons ( --kit-side-wc wide) and expands it again. The choice is <html data-kit-sidebar=\"collapsed|expanded\"> and is remembered, like theme and text size. To start compact just write the attribute in the HTML. Texts, badges, arrows and sub-items disappear. Hovering the mouse or moving focus with Tab onto an icon, its name appears right next to it (with the badge number, for example \"Alerts (3)\"); this applies to items, utilities and the account. The name is taken from the item's kit-side-text or, for icon buttons, from their aria-label . Each item also gets an aria-label by itself, because the hidden text does not reach screen readers. Pressing an item with sub-items expands it again. Kit.reset() and the data-kit-reset button restore the state written in the HTML.","--kit-side-wc data-kit-sidebar kit-side-text Kit.reset data-kit-reset"],["sidebar","Sidebar","subitems","Items with sub-items","An item with a submenu is a <details class=\"kit-side-details\"> with <summary class=\"kit-side-link\"> : it works without JavaScript and with the keyboard. The arrow is kit-side-chev ; the sub-items are a second kit-side-nav kit-side-sub . Invoices Received Issued Customers","kit-side-details kit-side-link kit-side-chev kit-side-nav kit-side-sub kit-app kit-sidebar kit-sidebar-body kit-icon kit-side-text"],["sidebar","Sidebar","account","Account and utilities at the bottom","In kit-sidebar-foot go the utilities ( kit-side-tools : icon buttons, settings, help) and the account. The account is kit-side-user with kit-side-avatar (the initials) and kit-side-user-text (name and secondary line); its menu is a normal pop-up menu opened upwards with kit-pop-up . <div class=\"kit-sidebar-foot\"> <div class=\"kit-dropdown\"> <button class=\"kit-side-user\" data-kit-toggle=\"#account\" aria-haspopup=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\"> <span class=\"kit-side-avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">MR</span> <span class=\"kit-side-user-text\"><b>Maria Smith</b><small>maria@example.com</small></span> </button> <div class=\"kit-pop kit-pop-up\" id=\"account\" role=\"menu\" hidden> <a class=\"kit-opt\" role=\"menuitem\" href=\"#\">Profile</a> <button class=\"kit-opt kit-opt-danger\" role=\"menuitem\">Sign out</button> </div> </div> </div>","kit-sidebar-foot kit-side-tools kit-side-user kit-side-avatar kit-side-user-text kit-pop-up kit-code data-kit-code kit-dropdown data-kit-toggle kit-pop kit-opt kit-opt-danger"],["sidebar","Sidebar","js","JavaScript","What Effect data-kit-sidebar-toggle=\"#id\" Button: opens or closes the slide-in sidebar, or compresses or expands the inline one. Without a value it acts on the first .kit-sidebar . aria-expanded updates by itself. Kit.sidebar.get() · set(\"collapsed|expanded\") · toggle() The compact state, remembered. Kit.sidebar.open(selector) · close(selector) The slide-in sidebar; they do nothing if it is inline. kit:sidebar event On the sidebar (bubbles): detail is { collapsed, open } .","kit-table data-kit-sidebar-toggle kit-sidebar Kit.sidebar"],["sidebar","Sidebar","tokens","Tokens and print","--kit-side-w (16.5rem): width of the bar; --kit-side-wc (4.667rem): width of the compact one. They can be overridden on :root or on a single .kit-app . When printing the sidebar disappears, like the header.","--kit-side-w --kit-side-wc kit-app"],["snippets","VS Code snippets","","VS Code snippets","Type the prefix and press Tab: the editor writes the component's markup, with the fields to fill in.",""],["snippets","VS Code snippets","installation","Installation","One project only : copy vscode/dashboard-kit.code-snippets into the project's .vscode/ folder. All projects : in VS Code open Preferences: Configure Snippets → New Global Snippets file and paste the file's content. Then, in an .html file, type for example kit-card and press Tab. With kit-page you get a whole page; with kit-dash the layout of a dashboard (KPIs, chart with side panel, table).","kit-card kit-page kit-dash"],["snippets","VS Code snippets","list","List of prefixes","Prefix Component kit-accordion Accordion with openable items (details), optionally only one open kit-alert Alert with colored border (success, warning, danger, neutral) kit-alert-close Alert with a close button kit-alert-icon Alert with icon (the symbol must be in the SVG sprite) kit-badge Badge (success, warning, danger, neutral) kit-bar Bar of side-by-side elements (toolbar, filters) kit-breadcrumb Navigation path (breadcrumb) kit-btn Button (variants: primary, ghost, danger, icon, lg) kit-btn-icon Square button with an icon only (SVG sprite) kit-btn-primary Primary button kit-card Card with header, body and footer kit-chart Bar chart in SVG (requires kit.js) kit-check-cards Radio buttons as cards kit-chip Removable chip kit-code Highlighted code block (with Copy button) kit-col Grid column (12 on phone, N/12 from a breakpoint) kit-combo Field with a list of suggestions (requires kit.js) kit-container Centered container (follows the data-layout switch; -boxed always centered) kit-container-fluid Container that is always full width kit-control Field with an icon on the left and a button on the right (also show/hide password) kit-dash Typical scheme: KPIs on top, chart + side panel","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-accordion kit-alert kit-alert-close kit-alert-icon kit-badge kit-bar kit-breadcrumb kit-btn kit-btn-icon kit-btn-primary kit-chart kit-check-cards kit-chip kit-code kit-col kit-combo kit-container kit-container-fluid kit-control kit-dash kit-date kit-daterange kit-datetime kit-dialog kit-dropdown kit-empty kit-field kit-float kit-form kit-form-h kit-grid kit-grid-2 kit-grid-3 kit-header kit-header-container kit-icon kit-icons kit-input-group kit-kpi kit-kv kit-layout kit-layout-toggle kit-list kit-meter kit-navbar kit-page kit-pill kit-progress kit-prose kit-quote kit-row kit-row-cols kit-search kit-seg kit-select kit-settings kit-sidebar"],["tables","Tables","","Tables","Compact tables with a sticky header, selectable rows and aligned numbers.",""],["tables","Tables","base","Table","Put the table in a card, inside kit-table-wrap , which makes it scroll horizontally on narrow screens. kit-num aligns right and gives the digits the same width; kit-wrap lets the text wrap. Date Number Customer Amount 03/12/2026 FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd VAT no. 01234567890 1,250.00 03/02/2026 FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 830.40 02/21/2026 FT-0040 Gamma Transport −310.00","kit-table-wrap kit-num kit-wrap kit-card kit-table kit-danger"],["tables","Tables","rows","Clickable and selected rows","kit-table-hover highlights the row under the mouse; is-selected on the <tr> marks it as chosen (useful with the side panel ). Number Status FT-0042 Issued FT-0041 Received FT-0040 Discarded","kit-table-hover kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-badge-warning kit-badge-danger"],["tables","Tables","sorting","Sorting","With kit.js , data-kit-sort on the table makes the headers clickable: the first click sorts ascending, the second descending, the third restores the starting order. The header gets aria-sort ( ascending , descending , none ) and a button is placed inside it, so it also works from the keyboard. The column type is recognized from its content: numbers in the page language's format (in English 1,250.00 , −310.00 , 12 % , € 5 ; in Italian 1.250,00 ), dates ( 03/12/2026 in English, 12/03/2026 in Italian, 2026-03-12 , with the time if present) and text , compared ignoring case and accents and with \"natural\" numbers ( FT-9 before FT-10 ). Empty cells, or cells with just a dash, always go to the bottom; with equal values the starting order is kept. An aria-sort=\"ascending|descending\" written in the HTML is the initial sort. Date Number Customer Amount 03/12/2026 FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd 1,250.00 03/02/2026 FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 830.40 02/21/2026 FT-0040 Gamma Transport −310.00 02/14/2026 FT-0039 Élite Consulting 12,400.00 02/03/2026 FT-0038 Delta Systems 95.50 01/28/2026 FT-0037 Alpha Services Ltd 2,100.00 01/19/2026 FT-0036 Zeta Logistics −45.00 01/09/2026 FT-0035 Beta Supplies Inc 1","data-kit-sort kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-num kit-danger data-kit-nosort data-kit-type data-kit-value"],["tables","Tables","sorting-multi","Several columns","With data-kit-sort=\"multi\" you can also sort by several columns together: Shift + click or Ctrl/⌘ + click on the header adds it as the next criterion (and again reverses it, and then removes it), while a normal click starts over from that column alone. The first criterion is the main one, the others decide ties; with several criteria the priority number appears next to the arrow. From the keyboard, Shift + Enter on the header button. Try it: Customer, then Shift + click on Amount. Date Number Customer Amount 03/12/2026 FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd 1,250.00 03/02/2026 FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 830.40 02/21/2026 FT-0040 Gamma Transport −310.00 02/14/2026 FT-0039 Élite Consulting 12,400.00 02/03/2026 FT-0038 Delta Systems 95.50 01/28/2026 FT-0037 Alpha Services Ltd 2,100.00 01/19/2026 FT-0036 Zeta Logistics −45.00 01/09/2026 FT-0035 Beta Supplies Inc 1,980.00 12/22/2025 FT-0034 Omega Studio 410.00 12/11/2025 FT-0033 Gamma Transport 75.20 11/30/2025 FT-0032 Delta Systems 3,300.00 11/15/2025 FT-0031 Élite Consulting 620.00 The small text ( <small> ) in a cell does not take part in sorting. With Kit.table you can also sort from code ( api.sort(2, \"descending\") , or api.sort([[2, \"ascending","data-kit-sort kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-num kit-danger Kit.table"],["tables","Tables","filter","Text filter","data-kit-filter=\"#id\" on a text field links the field to the table with that id: as you type, the rows that contain all the words remain (in any cell, ignoring case and accents). If nothing remains a \"No results\" row appears ( data-kit-empty on the table to change the text). Sorting and filtering work together; the event is kit:filter with { query, count } . Date Number Customer Amount 03/12/2026 FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd 1,250.00 03/02/2026 FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 830.40 02/21/2026 FT-0040 Gamma Transport −310.00 02/14/2026 FT-0039 Élite Consulting 12,400.00 02/03/2026 FT-0038 Delta Systems 95.50 01/28/2026 FT-0037 Alpha Services Ltd 2,100.00 01/19/2026 FT-0036 Zeta Logistics −45.00 01/09/2026 FT-0035 Beta Supplies Inc 1,980.00 12/22/2025 FT-0034 Omega Studio 410.00 12/11/2025 FT-0033 Gamma Transport 75.20 11/30/2025 FT-0032 Delta Systems 3,300.00 11/15/2025 FT-0031 Élite Consulting 620.00","data-kit-filter data-kit-empty kit-search --kit-sp kit-icon kit-input kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-sort kit-num kit-danger"],["tables","Tables","pagination","Pagination","data-kit-page=\"N\" on the table shows N rows at a time and adds the kit-pagination bar below: the count (\"1–5 of 12\"), the previous and next buttons and the page numbers with ellipses when there are many. The current page has aria-current=\"page\" , the count is an aria-live area and focus stays on the pressed button. It works together with sorting and filtering: changing either returns to the first page, and the count is that of the filtered rows. When printing the bar is not there and the page shown is printed. Date Number Customer Amount 03/12/2026 FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd 1,250.00 03/02/2026 FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 830.40 02/21/2026 FT-0040 Gamma Transport −310.00 02/14/2026 FT-0039 Élite Consulting 12,400.00 02/03/2026 FT-0038 Delta Systems 95.50 01/28/2026 FT-0037 Alpha Services Ltd 2,100.00 01/19/2026 FT-0036 Zeta Logistics −45.00 01/09/2026 FT-0035 Beta Supplies Inc 1,980.00 12/22/2025 FT-0034 Omega Studio 410.00 12/11/2025 FT-0033 Gamma Transport 75.20 11/30/2025 FT-0032 Delta Systems 3,300.00 11/15/2025 FT-0031 Élite Consulting 620.00 If the server does the pagination (the pages arrive ready-made) you write the bar by hand and use only the CSS: the buttons are normal kit","data-kit-page kit-pagination kit-search --kit-sp kit-icon kit-input data-kit-filter kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-table-hover data-kit-sort kit-num kit-danger kit-btn --kit-line --kit-rad kit-pagination-info kit-pagination-pages kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-pagination-gap"],["tables","Tables","htmx","With Django and htmx","When there are many records the server does pagination, sorting and filtering, one page at a time, and data-kit-sort , data-kit-filter and data-kit-page are not needed: they work on the rows already present. Only the CSS is used ( kit-pagination , kit-sort-btn , aria-sort ) and htmx replaces the block. If kit.js is present, fragments inserted by htmx initialize by themselves ( htmx:load event): selects, comboboxes, tabs, highlighted code and sortable tables inside the response work without calling Kit.init . The scheme: a container with an id ( #invoices ) that is the hx-target and holds the card with table and bar; the search field sits outside , so it is not replaced and the cursor stays where it is. hx-boost on the container turns normal links (headers, pages) into htmx requests with the browser history; the links keep working even without JavaScript. The full page ( invoices/list.html ) contains the field and the container; the view responds with only the fragment ( invoices/_table.html ) to htmx requests. <!-- invoices/list.html --> <input class=\"kit-input\" type=\"search\" name=\"q\" value=\"{{ q }}\" placeholder=\"Search invoices…\" aria-label=\"Search invoices\" hx-get=\"{% url 'invoic","data-kit-sort data-kit-filter data-kit-page kit-pagination kit-sort-btn Kit.init kit-code data-kit-code kit-input kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-table-empty kit-pagination-info kit-pagination-pages kit-btn kit-btn-ghost kit-btn-icon kit-pagination-gap kit-sort-n"],["tables","Tables","api","JavaScript","Attributes are enough in most cases. If the rows change after loading (a table filled by a request) call api.refresh() ; otherwise Kit.table(table, options) does everything from code and Kit.paginate(table, rows) is the shortcut for pagination only. Both return the same object. const api = Kit.table(\"#invoices\", { sort: true, size: 10, empty: \"No invoices\" }); api.sort(3, \"descending\"); // column (from 0) and direction: \"ascending\", \"descending\" or \"none\" api.sort([[2, \"ascending\"], [3, \"descending\"]]); // several columns (with data-kit-sort=\"multi\") api.filter(\"alfa\"); // like typing in the search field api.page(2); // go to page 2; api.page() reads it api.pageSize(25); // rows per page; 0 = all api.refresh(); // after adding, removing or changing rows api.state(); // { sort: { column, direction, criteria }, query, page, pages, size, total, count } document.querySelector(\"#invoices\").addEventListener(\"kit:page\", (e) => { console.log(e.detail); // { page, pages, size, total } }); Option Attribute Default sort data-kit-sort active only if the attribute is present size data-kit-page 0 : no pagination empty data-kit-empty No results labels – bar texts: of , prev , next , page (con {n}","Kit.table Kit.paginate kit-code data-kit-code data-kit-sort kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table data-kit-page data-kit-empty"],["tables","Tables","sticky","Sticky header and columns","By default the headers ( <th> ) stay stuck under .kit-header while the page scrolls. Inside kit-table-wrap the box scrolls only horizontally, so the header has nothing to detach from. For a long table add kit-table-scroll to the box: it has a maximum height ( --kit-table-h , by default 28rem ), also scrolls vertically and the header stays attached to its top edge. Cell spacing is adjusted with --kit-row (vertical) and --kit-cell (horizontal). kit-table-fix on the table locks the first column on the left while scrolling horizontally. It works with CSS only, even on rows added later (for example by htmx), and goes well with highlighted and selected rows. The corner cell (header of the fixed column) stays above everything. Try scrolling the table from one side to the other. Number Customer Date Net VAT Total Status Due date Notes FT-0042 Alpha Services Ltd 03/12/2026 1,025.41 225.59 1,251.00 Issued 04/11/2026 Payment in 30 days FT-0041 Beta Supplies Inc 03/02/2026 680.66 149.74 830.40 Received 04/01/2026 Partial delivery FT-0040 Gamma Transport 02/21/2026 −254.10 −55.90 −310.00 Discarded – Credit note FT-0039 Élite Consulting 02/14/2026 10,163.93 2,236.07 12,400.00 Issued 03/16/2026 A","kit-header kit-table-wrap kit-table-scroll --kit-table-h --kit-row --kit-cell kit-table-fix kit-card kit-table kit-table-hover kit-num kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-badge-warning kit-danger kit-badge-danger data-kit-fix --kit-fix-1 --kit-fix-2"],["theming","Themes and tokens","","Themes and tokens","The whole look comes from a few CSS variables. Changing them in :root , or on a single element, changes colors, density and corners of the whole interface.",""],["theming","Themes and tokens","theme","Light and dark theme","Colors are written once with light-dark(light, dark) . By default the theme follows the system; to force it set data-theme on <html> . With kit.js buttons with data-kit-theme-set are enough (the choice is remembered); the same goes for the settings panel , which gathers them with text and width. <html lang=\"en\" data-theme=\"dark\"> <!-- forced dark; without the attribute it follows the system --> <button class=\"kit-btn\" data-kit-theme-set=\"light\">Light</button> <button class=\"kit-btn\" data-kit-theme-set=\"dark\">Dark</button> <button class=\"kit-btn\" data-kit-theme-set=\"auto\">Automatic</button>","data-kit-theme-set kit-code data-kit-code kit-btn"],["theming","Themes and tokens","selector","Theme selector (menu)","The header's \"Theme\" menu is a pop-up menu ( .kit-pop ) whose items have data-kit-theme-set : on click kit.js applies the theme, remembers it and closes the menu. Each item has an icon and a title, and can have a gray line; kit-pop-right aligns the panel to the right edge, useful in a header. This example is really wired to the page's theme. Theme Automatic Follows the system Light Dark Add <meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"> in the <head> to avoid a white flash on load in the dark theme.","kit-pop data-kit-theme-set kit-pop-right kit-dropdown kit-btn data-kit-toggle kit-icon kit-opt kit-opt-text kit-opt-check"],["theming","Themes and tokens","text","Font and text size","The kit uses Inter (OFL license, 65 KB, file dist/fonts/inter-var.woff2 ), designed for the screen and with a slashed zero that is not confused with the letter \"o\". The file sits next to kit.css and loads by itself; if it is not reachable the system font remains. To use another font just change --kit-font ; for the slashed digit alone, font-variant-numeric: slashed-zero works with any font that provides it. :root { --kit-font: \"IBM Plex Sans\", system-ui, sans-serif; } /* another font */ td.code { font-variant-numeric: slashed-zero tabular-nums; } /* slashed zero and equal-width digits */ All text sizes are in rem , so they follow the base size --kit-fs ( 1rem ). The base grows by itself with the screen: 15px up to 1279px, then 16px, 17px (from 1600px), 19px (from 1920px) and 22px (from 2560px). Control height, icons, header and content width are also in rem and grow along with the text. The user can enlarge or shrink everything: --kit-zoom multiplies the base and data-kit-fs on <html> sets it ( md normal, the default; lg large; xl extra large). With kit.js buttons with data-kit-fs-set or data-kit-fs-step are enough; the choice is remembered. These choices are also in the settings p","--kit-font kit-code data-kit-code --kit-fs --kit-zoom data-kit-fs data-kit-fs-set data-kit-fs-step kit-btn"],["theming","Themes and tokens","layout","Layout tokens","They adjust the interface's breathing room, the text size and the heading scale (see Typography ). Below 760px --kit-sp goes down from 16 to 8px. Token Value What it controls --kit-fs 15px base text size (1rem) --kit-lh 1.5 text line height --kit-h1 2.2rem h1 heading (and kit-fs-1) --kit-h2 1.75rem h2 heading (and kit-fs-2) --kit-h3 1.4rem h3 heading (and kit-fs-3) --kit-h4 1.2rem h4 heading (and kit-fs-4) --kit-h5 1.05rem h5 heading (and kit-fs-5) --kit-h6 1rem h6 heading (and kit-fs-6) --kit-zoom .875 multiplier chosen by the user: 0.875 (normal), 1, 1.125 --kit-sp 16px single spacing unit: margin, distance between cards, inner padding --kit-row 8px vertical padding of table rows --kit-cell 12px horizontal padding between columns --kit-rad 12px radius of surfaces: cards, dialogs, menus, code, toasts --kit-rad-sm 8px radius of controls: buttons, fields, segmented, menu items --kit-hh 4.8rem header height --kit-ctl 2.667rem height of buttons and fields --kit-container-w 80rem maximum width of centered content (.kit-container) --kit-side-w 16.5rem sidebar width (.kit-sidebar) --kit-side-wc 4.667rem width of the compact, icons-only sidebar","--kit-sp kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table --kit-fs --kit-lh --kit-h1 kit-fs-1 --kit-h2 kit-fs-2 --kit-h3 kit-fs-3 --kit-h4 kit-fs-4 --kit-h5 kit-fs-5 --kit-h6 kit-fs-6 --kit-zoom --kit-row --kit-cell --kit-rad --kit-rad-sm --kit-hh --kit-ctl --kit-container-w kit-container --kit-side-w kit-sidebar --kit-side-wc"],["theming","Themes and tokens","colors","Color tokens","Each color has a value for the light and for the dark theme. The kit's classes always use tokens, never fixed colors: changing a token changes it everywhere. Token Light Dark Use --kit-bg #f4f5f8 #0f1319 Page background --kit-card #fff #171d26 Background of cards, header, tables --kit-ink #18202c #e8edf4 Main text --kit-mute #5f6a7c #8d99ab Secondary text --kit-line #e4e8ee #262e3a Borders --kit-line-soft #eef1f5 #1f2630 Light borders, table rows --kit-hover #f1f5ff #1c2736 Background on mouse hover --kit-accent #2559d8 #6ea2ff Accent color (buttons, links, selection) --kit-accent-ink #fff #0b1220 Text on the accent --kit-accent-soft #e9effd #1b2a45 Soft accent background --kit-danger #b0301f #ff7d6e Errors, negative values --kit-success #147236 #4fca8b Positive outcome --kit-warning #8f5200 #f0b04e Warnings --kit-c1 #2f6fe4 #6ea2ff Chart series 1 --kit-c2 #e39320 #f2a84c Chart series 2 --kit-c3 #1b8f82 #4ccbbb Chart series 3 --kit-c4 #8a4fd1 #b88cf0 Chart series 4 --kit-hl-tag #116329 #7ee787 Code: tags and selectors --kit-hl-attr #0550ae #79c0ff Code: attributes and properties --kit-hl-str #0a3069 #a5d6ff Code: strings --kit-hl-kw #cf222e #ff7b72 Code: keywords --kit-hl-fn #8250d","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table --kit-bg --kit-card --kit-ink --kit-mute --kit-line --kit-line-soft --kit-hover --kit-accent --kit-accent-ink --kit-accent-soft --kit-danger --kit-success --kit-warning --kit-c1 --kit-c2 --kit-c3 --kit-c4 --kit-hl-tag --kit-hl-attr --kit-hl-str --kit-hl-kw --kit-hl-fn --kit-hl-num --kit-hl-com"],["theming","Themes and tokens","scrollbar","Scrollbars","All scrollbars (page, tables, menus, dialogs) are thin, with the thumb in the secondary text color and an invisible track. The color is the --kit-sb token, which follows the light and dark theme by itself. The kit-no-scrollbar class hides the scrollbar of an element that still scrolls (useful for a row of tabs on narrow screens). A scrolling box: the bar on the right is the kit's. Second line. Third line. Fourth line. Fifth line. Sixth line. :root { --kit-sb: color-mix(in srgb, var(--kit-accent) 50%, transparent); } /* another color */ * { scrollbar-width: auto; scrollbar-color: auto; } /* or the system's */","--kit-sb kit-no-scrollbar kit-card kit-p-3 kit-code data-kit-code --kit-accent"],["theming","Themes and tokens","customizing","Customizing","Override the tokens in :root after loading kit.css : :root { --kit-accent: light-dark(#0f766e, #5eead4); --kit-accent-soft: light-dark(#e6f6f4, #12312e); --kit-rad: 6px; /* less rounded surfaces */ --kit-rad-sm: 4px; /* less rounded controls */ --kit-row: 5px; /* more compact tables */ --kit-ctl: 36px; /* shorter buttons and fields */ } Tokens can also be changed on a single element, and apply to everything it contains. Here an area with another accent: Primary Active pill Badge A link Note: the inline style attribute requires style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline' if the site has a Content-Security-Policy; in a CSS file it is not needed.","kit-code data-kit-code --kit-accent --kit-accent-soft --kit-rad --kit-rad-sm --kit-row --kit-ctl kit-bar kit-btn kit-btn-primary kit-pill kit-badge"],["typography","Typography","","Typography","Headings, body text, quotes, lists and the classes to control size, weight, line height and line width. It all starts from a few tokens, so it is adjusted from a single place.",""],["typography","Typography","base","Base text","The kit uses the Inter font at 1rem with line height --kit-lh (1.5). 1rem is the base size --kit-fs , which grows with the screen and can be chosen by the user (see Font and text size ): all the sizes below are in rem or em , so they follow it. Zeros are slashed, so they are not confused with the letter \"o\".","--kit-lh --kit-fs"],["typography","Typography","headings","Headings","The <h1> … <h6> elements already have the kit's style. The kit-h1 … kit-h6 classes give the same look to another element (a <p> , a <div> ) without changing the document structure. A <small> inside the heading becomes a gray secondary text. h1. Page title h2. Section title h3. Group title h4. Block title h5. Small title h6. Smallest title With secondary text gray subtitle A paragraph that looks like an h4 (kit-h4) The sizes are the --kit-h1 … --kit-h6 tokens: changing them in :root changes the scale of the whole page, including the kit-fs-1 … kit-fs-6 classes. :root { --kit-h1: 2.6rem; /* bigger headings */ --kit-h2: 2rem; }","kit-h1 kit-h6 kit-h4 --kit-h1 --kit-h6 kit-fs-1 kit-fs-6 kit-code data-kit-code --kit-h2"],["typography","Typography","display","Display","For an opening title, bigger and lighter than the normal ones ( kit-display-1 is the largest, kit-display-4 the smallest). Below 576px they shrink by themselves. Display 1 Display 2 Display 3 Display 4","kit-display-1 kit-display-4 kit-display-2 kit-display-3"],["typography","Typography","lead","Lead paragraph","With kit-lead the first paragraph stands out from the rest. A lead paragraph: a bit bigger than normal text, to introduce the topic. The text that follows has the normal size.","kit-lead"],["typography","Typography","inline","Inline text","You can highlight a part ( <mark> ), delete ( <del> ), insert ( <ins> ), underline ( <u> ), make bold or italic , and write in smaller type ( <small> ). Abbreviations show their meaning on mouse hover: VAT , and in small caps with kit-initialism : html . For a key use Ctrl + K ; for code kit-card .","kit-initialism kit-card"],["typography","Typography","utilities","Classes to control the text","All with !important , like the utilities , to win over the components' style.",""],["typography","Typography","size","Size","kit-fs-1 … kit-fs-6 use the same scale as the headings; kit-fs-sm and kit-fs-lg are relative to the text that contains them ( .875em and 1.2em ), useful inside a component. kit-fs-1 kit-fs-2 kit-fs-3 kit-fs-4 kit-fs-5 kit-fs-6 Normal text, smaller (kit-fs-sm) and larger (kit-fs-lg) .","kit-fs-1 kit-fs-6 kit-fs-sm kit-fs-lg kit-lh-1 kit-fs-2 kit-fs-3 kit-fs-4 kit-fs-5"],["typography","Typography","weight","Weight and style","kit-fw-light — light (300) kit-fw-normal — normal (400) kit-fw-medium — medium (500) kit-fw-semibold — semibold (600) kit-fw-bold — bold (700) kit-fst-italic — italic kit-fst-normal — removes the italic","kit-fw-light kit-fw-normal kit-fw-medium kit-fw-semibold kit-fw-bold kit-fst-italic kit-fst-normal"],["typography","Typography","alignment","Alignment and wrapping","kit-left — left kit-center — center kit-right — right kit-nowrap: a long line that never wraps and so overflows the space kit-wrap: removes the ban on wrapping and the text goes back into the available space. kit-break: also breaks very long identifiers like IT01234567890ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789","kit-left kit-center kit-right kit-card kit-p-3 kit-nowrap kit-mute kit-wrap kit-break"],["typography","Typography","transforms","Case, decoration and spacing","kit-uppercase — all uppercase KIT-LOWERCASE — ALL LOWERCASE kit-capitalize — capitalized words kit-underline — underlined kit-line-through — struck through kit-no-underline — a link without underline kit-ls-tight — tighter letters kit-ls-wide — spaced letters","kit-uppercase kit-lowercase kit-capitalize kit-underline kit-line-through kit-no-underline kit-ls-tight kit-ls-wide kit-fs-sm"],["typography","Typography","line-height","Line height","kit-lh-1 (1), kit-lh-sm (1.25), kit-lh-base (the value of --kit-lh ) and kit-lh-lg (1.8). To change it everywhere just change --kit-lh . kit-lh-sm — A line of text long enough to wrap at least once, to see how close the lines are to each other. kit-lh-lg — A line of text long enough to wrap at least once, to see how close the lines are to each other.","kit-lh-1 kit-lh-sm kit-lh-base --kit-lh kit-lh-lg kit-row kit-col-12 kit-col-md-6"],["typography","Typography","family","Monospace font and color","kit-mono uses the code font ( --kit-mono ), useful for identifiers and amounts in a column. Text colors are in Utilities ; kit-ink brings back the normal color inside a colored element. FT-0042 · €1,250.00 · kit-mute kit-ink","kit-mono --kit-mono kit-ink kit-mute"],["typography","Typography","quotes","Quotes","With kit-quote on a <blockquote> : a bar in the accent color on the left. The source goes in a <footer> (or in a <figcaption> if the quote is inside a <figure> ), preceded by an em dash. A good dashboard shows the things you need, at the moment you need them. From the project notes","kit-quote"],["typography","Typography","lists","Lists","Normal Received invoices Issued invoices Credit notes kit-list-unstyled Received invoices Issued invoices Credit notes kit-list-inline Received Issued Notes For label/value detail lists there is key / value .","kit-row kit-col-12 kit-col-md-4 kit-fw-semibold kit-mute kit-fs-sm kit-list-unstyled kit-list-inline"],["typography","Typography","prose","Long texts","An article, a guide or some notes read better with shorter lines and more space between lines. kit-prose limits the width to --kit-measure (65 characters), brings the line height to 1.7 and spaces paragraphs, headings and lists regularly, without you having to put classes on the single elements. To limit only the width of a block there is kit-measure . How a long text is read When a line goes past about seventy characters the eye struggles to return to the start of the next line. This is why long texts should not take up the whole width of a large screen. Line height matters too: lines that are too close blur together, lines too far apart read as separate paragraphs. Some tips Keep lines under 65–75 characters. Use a line height between 1.5 and 1.7. Give headings more space above than below. <article class=\"kit-prose\"> <h2>Title</h2> <p>Text…</p> </article> :root { --kit-measure: 72ch; } /* slightly longer lines */","kit-prose --kit-measure kit-measure kit-code data-kit-code"],["typography","Typography","tokens","Typographic tokens","Token Value What it controls --kit-font \"Kit Inter\", system-ui, … Text font --kit-mono ui-monospace, Consolas, … Code font --kit-fs 15px Base size (1rem), grows with the screen --kit-zoom .875 Multiplier chosen by the user --kit-lh 1.5 Text line height --kit-measure 65ch Maximum length of a line ( kit-prose , kit-measure ) --kit-h1 … --kit-h6 2.2rem … 1rem Size of headings and of kit-fs-1 … kit-fs-6","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table --kit-font --kit-mono --kit-fs --kit-zoom --kit-lh --kit-measure kit-prose kit-measure --kit-h1 --kit-h6 kit-fs-1 kit-fs-6"],["utilities","Utilities","","Utilities","One-line classes, as in Bootstrap: spacing, display, flexbox, sizes, text and visibility. Almost all use !important to win over components.",""],["utilities","Utilities","spacing","Margins and padding","Format kit-{m|p}{side}-{n} . Sides: none (all), t top, b bottom, s start, e end, x horizontal, y vertical. The n scale goes from 0 to 5; margins also have auto . n 0 1 2 3 4 5 Value 0 4px 8px 16px 24px 48px p-0 p-1 p-2 p-3 p-4 px-5 py-2 kit-mt-4 kit-mb-2 Left kit-ms-auto: to the right","kit-card kit-table-wrap kit-table kit-bar kit-p-0 kit-p-1 kit-p-2 kit-p-3 kit-p-4 kit-px-5 kit-py-2 kit-card-body kit-mt-4 kit-mb-2 kit-d-flex kit-btn kit-ms-auto"],["utilities","Utilities","display","Display","kit-d-{value} with value none , inline , block , inline-block , flex , inline-flex , grid . With a breakpoint it applies from there up: kit-d-md-none . Visible from md (768px) up: kit-d-none kit-d-md-block Visible only below md: kit-d-md-none Resize the window to see the two boxes alternate.","kit-d kit-d-md-none kit-stack kit-card kit-p-3 kit-d-none kit-d-md-block kit-mute"],["utilities","Utilities","flex","Flexbox","With kit-d-flex you enable direction ( kit-flex-row , -column , -row-reverse , -column-reverse ), wrapping ( kit-flex-wrap , -nowrap ), kit-justify-content-{start|end|center|between|around|evenly} , kit-align-items-{start|end|center|baseline|stretch} , kit-align-self-* , kit-flex-grow-1 , kit-flex-shrink-0 , kit-flex-fill and kit-gap-0…5 . Direction, justify and align also have a per-breakpoint version. Title justify-content-between Does not shrink flex-grow-1: takes the remaining space In a column on the phone in a row from md up","kit-d-flex kit-flex-row kit-flex-wrap kit-justify-content kit-align-items kit-align-self kit-flex-grow-1 kit-flex-shrink-0 kit-flex-fill kit-gap-0 kit-stack kit-justify-content-between kit-align-items-center kit-card kit-p-3 kit-badge kit-badge-success kit-gap-3 kit-btn kit-flex-column kit-flex-md-row kit-gap-2"],["utilities","Utilities","sizing","Sizes","kit-w-100 , kit-w-auto , kit-h-100 , kit-h-auto . kit-h-100 is often needed to make a card reach the height of the column that contains it.","kit-w-100 kit-w-auto kit-h-100 kit-h-auto"],["utilities","Utilities","text","Text and color","kit-mute kit-accent kit-success kit-warning kit-danger 1,234.50 (kit-num: aligned digits) kit-truncate cuts with an ellipsis a text that is too long for the available space Others: kit-nowrap , kit-center , kit-right . Size, weight, line height, case and line width are in Typography .","kit-bar kit-mute kit-accent kit-success kit-warning kit-danger kit-num kit-card kit-p-3 kit-mt-3 kit-truncate kit-nowrap kit-center kit-right"],["utilities","Utilities","visibility","Visibility","kit-hidden and the hidden attribute: hide the element. kit-sr : hides it visually but it stays readable by screen readers (labels for icon-only controls). kit-hide-sm (below 760px) and kit-only-sm (only below 760px): shortcuts tied to the phone breakpoint. For the other breakpoints use kit-d-* .","kit-hidden kit-sr kit-hide-sm kit-only-sm kit-d"],["utilities","Utilities","print","Print","The kit prepares the page for printing: always on light (even if it is dark on screen), without header, alerts and tabs, without shadows, with the page margins reset. Badge and chart colors are kept. Cards, lists, KPI cards and table rows do not split between two pages, and the table header repeats on every page. kit-no-print : the element is not printed (buttons, filters, toolbars). kit-print-only : the element is only visible when printing (document title, date, notes). kit-print-break : goes to a new page; kit-print-avoid : does not split between two pages. The sheet size and margins are left to the app: @page { size: A4; margin: 14mm } in your CSS.","kit-no-print kit-print-only kit-print-break kit-print-avoid"],["dashboard","Dashboard","","Dashboard","Complete example: a dashboard built with the kit.","kit-header kit-card kit-kpi kit-table"],["dashboard-sidebar","Dashboard with sidebar","","Dashboard with sidebar","Complete example: a left sidebar with header, sub-items, account and utilities.","kit-app kit-sidebar kit-side-link kit-header"]];
